window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":326,"title":"Chapter 326: Eavesdropping","paragraphs":["\"Nah, Noah wouldn’t do that.\" Leonard spoke up for him. \"No matter how playful he can be, flirting with a woman old enough to be his mother isn’t something he’d do.\"","Noah immediately nodded. \"Exactly! How could I ever do something like that?\"","Lyria also nodded in agreement. \"I think so too. No matter how much of a tease Noah may be, I don’t think he would ever do something like that to an older woman.\"","Noah felt a little relieved hearing Lyria defend him. ’At least Lyria believes in me.’","Arisha, however, remained unconvinced.","She narrowed her yellow eyes at him for another moment before eventually returning her attention to her food.","\"Well, whatever. I still think you did something, but I’ll let it go.\"","She shrugged indifferently. \"It’s not my problem, anyway.\"","Noah felt a strange bitterness at her words. ’Why does it feel like she’s already decided I’m guilty?’","Still, there was no point in continuing the conversation. He quickly decided to change the subject.","\"So, what’s going to be different during our second semester?\"","\"No idea,\" Damien replied. \"Classes begin tomorrow, so I guess we’ll find out.\"","Draven immediately let out a heavy sigh. \"Ugh... boring classes. Lectures...\"","He looked thoroughly displeased.","Draven clearly preferred practical lessons where he could train, fight, and actually use his strength rather than sit through hours of lectures.","\"I understand you, brother.\"","Ragnar nodded seriously. The two of them clearly shared the same hatred for studying.","The group continued chatting while finishing their lunch, enjoying their first reunion after Noah’s long absence.","---","Later, Noah parted ways with his friends.","He had no particular plans for the rest of the afternoon, so he decided to return to his dormitory and rest for a while.","He had barely walked halfway there when he noticed someone familiar in the distance.","A young man with black hair was walking ahead of him.","Ken Takeane was also from the Raigamine Duchy, the Eastern Duchy where Akari came from.","He and Noah were classmates, and they had fought alongside each other during several practical exercises before.","Since they already knew each other, Noah decided to greet him. But before Noah could call out to him, Ken suddenly turned onto another path.","Noah stopped.","’...Huh?’","Ken was heading toward the back of the dormitory building.","That was the same area where Noah had previously made a deal with Travis and the others before their VR match.","’Why is he going there?’","Noah frowned. Something about Ken’s behavior felt strange. He glanced around before quietly moving toward the large bushes lining both sides of the path.","He crouched behind them and waited.","Ken continued walking. After a short distance, he suddenly stopped. Then he slowly turned around.","His eyes swept across the surroundings. He carefully checked the area, making sure no one was following him.","Noah remained completely still.","’He’s checking whether someone is watching him... good thing I hide, after all no one goes to that place...’","Ken seemed satisfied that he was alone and continued toward the back of the dormitory.","Noah narrowed his eyes. ’Something’s definitely wrong.’","He hadn’t remembered Ken being particularly suspicious before. In fact, Ken had fought alongside them during their practical examination against the demons.","’Does he have some kind of important role in the game?’","The thought immediately crossed Noah’s mind. His curiosity won. He decided to follow him.","Noah quietly made his way around the dormitory and reached the rear compound wall.","He carefully hid behind it and peeked around the corner.","Ken was there. But he wasn’t alone.","Another person was standing with him.","Noah recognized her almost immediately.","\"You finally came back.\"","A familiar female voice reached his ears.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","’Marina Lumineth.’","It was the elf girl who had been part of Noah’s group during the Oakhaven field trip, when they had gone into the wilderness to hunt monsters.","Marina looked relieved to see Ken.","\"Sigh... So, how did things go?\"","\"Better than expected.\"","Ken reached into his belongings.","\"Take this.\"","Noah remained hidden behind the wall. He couldn’t see what Ken had handed her.","Marina stared at the object in her hands. \"Th-This is really an Everbloom Draught?!\"","Her voice trembled with disbelief. \"You actually found one?! How?\"","\"Don’t ask.\" Ken let out a tired sigh. \"I went through a lot of trouble to get it during the vacation.\"","Despite his exhausted tone, Noah could hear a faint hint of satisfaction in his voice.","Marina stared at the potion as though it were a priceless treasure.","\"With this...\" Her voice suddenly became emotional. \"With this, my sister can be cured.\"","\"Huh?!\"","Ken’s voice suddenly became flustered. \"Wait, Marina! Why are you hugging me?!\"","\"Thank you... Thank you, Ken!\"","Marina’s voice trembled as she hugged him tightly.","\"Because of you, my sister can run around again!\"","It sounded as though she was crying.","Noah remained hidden behind the wall.","’Ah... I get it.’","Everything seemed to make sense now.","’Marina must have a younger sister suffering from some kind of illness that can be treated with a rare potion. Ken went through all that trouble to obtain the Everbloom Draught for her.’","Noah nodded to himself.","’That’s why she’s so emotional.’","However something still didn’t feel right. He continued listening.","\"Thank you...\"","Marina’s voice became quieter.","\"I’ll do whatever you want.\"","\"Sure.\"","Ken’s response was calm.","\"But first, give the potion to your sister. Once she’s actually cured, then you can help me.\"","\"Yes.\"","Marina hesitated before continuing.","\"But... to be honest, it’s not going to be easy to arrange a meeting between you and the Elven Queen.\"","Noah’s expression immediately changed.","’...What?’","\"She’s like an elder sister to me,\" Marina continued.","\"And my family is one of the most loyal houses to the royal family. But even so, I can’t guarantee that Her Majesty will agree to meet you.\"","\"Just try.\"","Ken’s voice became serious.","\"You’re the only hope I have.\"","Marina fell silent for a moment.","\"But why do you want to meet Her Majesty?\"","\"It’s something important.\"","Ken’s voice became guarded.","\"I can’t tell you right now.\"","He paused. \"And as a commoner, I have no way of contacting her directly.\"","Noah remained completely silent behind the wall.","His expression gradually became more serious.","’Okay...’","He had initially thought this was simply a matter of Marina’s sister being sick.","But now. ’This is weird.’","Ken had gone through considerable trouble to obtain an extremely rare potion for Marina.","In exchange, he wanted her help arranging a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And whatever he wanted to discuss with her was apparently important enough that he refused to tell Marina about it.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","’I have no idea what’s going on...’","His curiosity grew stronger.","’And what exactly does Ken Takeane want with the Elven Queen? Does he know about something? or does he have future knowledge? Damn what a coincident I found myself into!!’","---","IMPORTANT RANTT OF AUTHOR!!","[A/N: Hello, guys! This is for all the readers who are still sticking with my novel. I genuinely thank you all from the bottom of my heart. If you’re still reading at this point, that means we probably share a similar taste in stories and novels, haha!","Well, I know my last arc involving Akari might have been pretty bad since I stretched it out for quite a while. I apologize for that. I also know that some of you might not like the idea of her joining the harem.","But honestly, I had already decided this a long time ago. So, if you’re still reading, I guess that means you don’t mind it too much. This novel was always meant to be a harem novel, since, well... I’m a harem novel reader myself, haha! Personally, I don’t really like small harems with only two or three girls I’d rather just write a novel with a single FL. Still I’ve decided to limit the harem to five girls for this novel.","Sigh... Anyway, to those of you who are disappointed or sad about this development, I’m sorry. But at the end of the day, I’m writing the story I personally enjoy. If you like this kind of story, I hope you’ll continue reading and enjoying it. And if it’s not your cup of tea, I won’t force you to keep reading.","As for why I’m saying all this... Well, sometimes we authors also feel down and start questioning whether we should continue writing a book or not. So, I just wanted to share a little bit of what was on my mind. Thank you again to everyone who has stayed with the novel this far. I really appreciate you all! ]"]},{"number":327,"title":"Chapter 327: Browsing Information [1]","paragraphs":["\"Well, let’s meet again later. I’m exhausted and need to get some rest.\"","Ken’s voice reached Noah from the other side of the wall.","’They’re leaving!’","Noah immediately stopped listening. He didn’t want to risk being discovered.","\"Yes, of course. Let’s go.\"","The two of them began walking.","Noah carefully slipped away from the area.","He moved through the bushes without making a sound and only relaxed once he had reached a considerable distance from the dormitory.","He finally let out a quiet breath.","\"Okay...\"","Noah rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","\"Ken is definitely hiding something.\"","He hadn’t known Ken particularly well before, but what he had witnessed today was enough to make him suspicious.","Ken had secretly met Marina behind the dormitory, handed her an extremely rare potion, and in exchange, asked her to arrange a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And whatever he wanted to discuss with the queen was apparently so important that he wasn’t even willing to tell Marina about it.","Noah thought about it for a moment.","’He gave Marina that Everbloom Draught...’","His eyes narrowed.","’What exactly does that potion do?’","If it was valuable enough for Ken to go through considerable trouble to obtain it during his vacation, there had to be more to it.","’I should find out.’","Noah decided to return to his dormitory.","’I can search for information about it on the internet. There should be something about a potion that rare.’","Back inside his dormitory, Noah lay comfortably on his bed with his phone in hand.","Nancy was curled up beside him, peacefully sleeping.","Noah, however, was far too curious to rest. He opened his browser and began searching. He was lucky that the information about this potion existed there, not hidden like some ancient treasure.","\"Everbloom Draught...\"","He scrolled through one page after another.","The potion was more known to world that he thought. No wonder it’s information existed online.","There were articles about rare potions, alchemical records, medical references, historical documents, and discussions written by adventurers and scholars.","Noah continued reading.","\"Hmm...\"","His expression gradually became more serious.","\"It’s really rare...\"","According to several sources, the Everbloom Draught was an exceptionally difficult potion to produce. Even among high-level healing potions, it was considered a precious item because of the number of severe conditions it could treat.","Noah continued scrolling.","\"It can cure several dangerous diseases...\"","He paused.","\"But which one is considered the most dangerous?\"","His eyes moved down the page. Then he stopped. \"Bloodmoon Rot...\"","The name immediately caught his attention.","Noah clicked on the article and began reading carefully.","Bloodmoon Rot was one of the rarest blood-related disease that gradually corrupted the victim’s bloodstream.","As the disease progressed, crimson-colored veins would begin spreading across the victim’s body. The victim would experience an intense and unnatural thirst, recurring high fever, severe weakness, and eventually the failure of vital organs.","Ordinary medicine and conventional antidotes were completely ineffective against it.","Once the disease reached an advanced stage, death was almost inevitable.","Then Noah noticed the treatment.","Treatment: Everbloom Draught","The potion could completely purify the corrupted blood and eliminate the disease from the victim’s body.","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\"This is...\"","He continued reading.","Then he reached the section describing the origin of the disease.","Known Cause: Vampires.","According to historical and medical records, certain highborn vampires from House Bloodwyn possessed a rare ability to infect their enemies with Bloodmoon Rot. Rather than killing their victims immediately, they could cause their blood to slowly deteriorate, allowing the disease to consume the victim over time.","Noah stared at the screen.","His expression slowly changed.","’Vampires...’","That single word caught his attention far more than anything else on the page.","’If Marina’s sister has this disease...’","His thoughts began connecting the pieces.","’That would mean she was infected by a highborn vampire.’","Noah frowned.","’But that doesn’t make sense.’","Vampires had been extinct for a century. At least, that was what history claimed.","Noah changed the tab of his browser and search for history about vampires. He does know few things from old Noah’s memory. Still he decided to read it again.","The Kingdom of Vespermark had once existed on an island near the Demon Continent.","It had been a small kingdom compared to the major human and elven nations, but the vampires who lived there were notoriously powerful.","Their natural regenerative abilities were extraordinary, and consuming blood allowed them to recover from injuries at an astonishing rate.","Even among supernatural races, vampires were feared for their physical resilience.","But their relationship with humanity and the elves had always been hostile.","Vampires particularly favored the blood of humans and elves, with the blood of high elves being considered especially valuable.","That hostility eventually led to a devastating war.","Humanity and the Elven Kingdom eventually joined forces against Vespermark.","The vampire kingdom was simply too small to withstand two major powers attacking it simultaneously.","Noah continued reading historical records about the conflict.","The war had ended with the complete destruction of Vespermark. The vampires had been hunted down and exterminated. Be it women, children or old people.","According to the historical records, neither side had shown mercy.","Noah’s fingers slowly tightened around his phone.","’They really wiped out the entire race...’","He imagined what that must have looked like.","An entire kingdom surrounded by two powerful nations. There was no realistic way for a small island kingdom to survive such an attack.","It wasn’t really a war anymore. It had become a complete defeat followed by the destruction of an entire people.","A shiver ran down Noah’s spine.","\"That’s... brutal.\"","’There has to be more to this history.’","Noah leaned back against the headboard.","’If vampires really went extinct nearly a hundred years ago, then how could Bloodmoon Rot still be appearing? Maybe Marina’s sister wasn’t suffering from Bloodmoon Rot at all or maybe some vampires from House Bloodwyn had survived.’","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","’If even one highborn vampire survived the destruction of Vespermark, then this changes everything.’","He immediately shook his head.","\"Don’t jump to conclusions.\"","He reminded himself.","’I don’t even know if Marina’s sister has Bloodmoon Rot.’","For all he knew, her illness could be completely unrelated.","Still, the coincidence was too strange to ignore.","Ken had gone through great trouble to obtain an Everbloom Draught.","Marina had said the potion could allow her sister to run around again.","Noah stared at the ceiling.","\"There’s definitely something going on. Let’s see where this potion could be found.\"","He went back to tab of potion’s information. \"The fuck!!\" He couldn’t help but curse after reading more information.","It was written that to make Everbloom Draught potion it needs blood of a highborn vampire who posses that ability to spread disease. It is essential ingredient.","Because of this in current time if there exist this potions in world, then they were extremely rare, biggest chance to found them were within dungeons made by vampires."]},{"number":328,"title":"Chapter 328: Browsing Information [2]","paragraphs":["He paused. \"I guess I need to study history more seriously too.\"","His curiosity had only grown. He wanted to know more about Vespermark.","More about the vampires.","Noah eventually sat up.","\"Enough thinking. Huge possibility that Ken might be like me... but with knowledge...\"","He placed his phone aside and got out of bed.","Nancy, who had been sleeping comfortably throughout his entire investigation, opened one golden eye because of the sound.","She watched Noah hurriedly walk toward his desk.","\"Meow...\"","Noah glanced back at her.","\"What?\"","Nancy stared at him for a few seconds.","Then she yawned lazily.","\"...\"","She simply closed her eyes again and went back to sleep.","Noah sighed.","\"Right. Of course. Why would you care?\"","He walked over to his desk. After sitting down, Noah reached into his storage ring and took out a thick notebook along with a pen.","This wasn’t an ordinary notebook. It was something Noah had started using specifically for dangerous information.","Whenever something suspicious happened to him, whenever he encountered an incident he couldn’t explain, or whenever he discovered something that might become important later, he wrote it down.","He had learned the hard way that relying entirely on memory was dangerous.","Especially in this world. Noah opened the notebook to a fresh page. He stared at the blank page for a moment.","Then he began writing. The first thing he recorded was the labyrinth.","He carefully documented everything he could remember from the moment he and Damien entered it.","From routes to monsters to the portal. Also the phenomenon happened after Noah vanished in portal.","How those creatures came out from the last boss’s body.","He wrote down every detail he could remember, even things that seemed insignificant.","He deliberately avoided writing anything in a vague manner. If he remembered something clearly, he wrote it down as fact.","After several pages, he reached the events involving Akari.","He carefully recorded how he had encountered her inside the mysterious realm and how they had eventually fought together to survive. he didn’t wrote anything about her bloodline.","He didn’t write down every single detail exactly as it had happened, but he made sure he had enough information to reconstruct the events later.","Eventually, he reached today’s events.","Noah turned to a new section.","Ken Takeane — Suspicious Activity","He began writing.","Ken Takeane was observed secretly meeting Marina behind the dormitory building.","After he was done he rubbed his forehead.","\"Why does everything around me have to be so complicated?\"","He sighed. Then his gaze drifted toward Nancy.","The black cat was still sleeping peacefully on his bed, completely unconcerned with the mysteries threatening to pile up around them.","Noah couldn’t help but smile. \"At least someone here has a peaceful life that I always wish.\"","Nancy’s ears twitched. But she didn’t open her eyes.","Noah kept staring at her then chuckled quietly. Then his expression became serious again.","He looked down at his notebook. \"I need to find out what Ken is planning.\"","He picked up his pen once more. \"And I need to find out whether Marina’s sister actually has Bloodmoon Rot.\"","If she did then the question wouldn’t simply be how she had contracted the disease.","The bigger question would be much more frightening. Were there still vampires alive in this world? If yes then definitely they have some dangerous role in future of this game, in future of this world.","Noah slowly closed the notebook.","Whatever the answer was, he had a feeling that this matter would eventually lead him somewhere he hadn’t expected.","----","\"Yes, Noah? Why did you call me?\"","\"Can’t I call you without a reason now?\" Noah asked, sounding genuinely hurt. \"Sigh... If you really want a reason, then it’s because I missed you.\"","He lay comfortably on his bed with Nancy resting on his chest. One hand gently stroked the little cat’s head, occasionally messing with her fur just to annoy her, while his other hand held the phone to his ear.","He was talking to one of the people dearest to him.","A soft chuckle came from the other end of the call.","\"Haha, don’t be so dramatic. And yes, you can call me even if you don’t have a reason. Just try not to do it when I’m busy.\"","It was Akari’s calm, familiar voice.","\"Hmm... I miss you.\"","\"Yes. Me too. So, did you go to the academy?\"","\"Yeah. Just today.\"","They continued talking for a while, jumping between random topics and casually sharing what had happened since they last spoke. Neither of them seemed particularly interested in ending the call.","After a while, however, Noah remembered the reason he’d wanted to speak with her.","\"Akari, I wanted to ask you something.\"","\"Sure. What is it?\"","\"Hmm...\" Noah hesitated for a moment before asking, \"Do you think vampires are still alive?\"","There was silence on the other end.","Akari didn’t say anything for a while. \"According to the records of our history...\" she finally began, her voice thoughtful, \"they’re supposed to be dead.\"","She continued \"But honestly, I wouldn’t completely believe those records. Vampires weren’t some unintelligent race of beasts or monsters that could simply disappear or get extinct from the world. They were an intelligent race, just like humans and elves.\"","Akari paused briefly.","\"Making an entire intelligent race completely disappear is almost impossible. So, I believe there are definitely some vampires still out there somewhere.\"","\"Hmm... okay.\"","\"But why the sudden interest in vampires?\"","\"Nothing serious. I was studying history and suddenly became curious about them. The war was really cruel.\"","\"Well, that’s how war is,\" Akari replied calmly. \"It happens between races, and sometimes even between humans themselves.\"","She paused before adding,","\"Don’t forget that my family and the Raigamine Duchy was once a separate kingdom. It was only after we lost a war against the Aurelian Empire that our kingdom became part of the empire.\"","\"Oh, right...\"","Noah fell silent for a moment, thinking about her words.","’So Akari also believes that the vampires might still be alive...’","His curiosity only deepened.","---","[A/N: Damn guys!! I actually forgot to upload Chapters yesterday!! I thought i uploaded but i didn’t!! Damn my goldfish memory!! Sorry!!]"]},{"number":329,"title":"Chapter 329: Away from Academy","paragraphs":["=== STATUS ===","Name: Noah Eldritch","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 724 [+112]","Speed: 737 [+120]","Stamina: 720 [+101]","Endurance: 712 [+104]","Charm: 803 [+103]","Mana: 7313 [+1100]","Core Rank: Condensed (High)","Potential: Mythical Core / Origin Core (???)","Profession: [Combatant Lv.3]","Technique: [Frozen Lotus Blade Art], [Flowing String Archery]","Affinity: Ice","Spells: [Ice Shard], [Frost Bind], [Snow Mist], [Ice Blizzard], [Crystal Bloom], [Winter Howl]","Innate Ability: [Ice Creation]","Passive Abilities: [Adaptive Learning], [Heart of Absolute Frost]","Active Ability: [Monarch’s Decree], [Puppet of the Frost Dragon]","Bloodline: [Monarch of the Frost]","===================","\"Damn, my powers have increased by quite a lot.\"","Noah looked over his status with satisfaction.","He had made tremendous progress in just six months since arriving in this world.","Well... technically, it had been much longer than six months.","He had spent seven months inside that mysterious realm, after all. But from the perspective of the outside world, only a month had passed.","And now, there was something else he wanted to try.","His newly acquired ability.","[Puppet of the Frost Dragon].","’How exactly does this Frost Dragon puppet work?’","He was eager to find out.","It was another morning, and today marked Noah’s first class of the second semester at Novaris Academy.","He glanced at the calendar.","Today was the 24th day of the sixth month, Year 2048.","After getting ready, Noah put on his academy uniform, a gray coat over a white shirt, accompanied by a red tie.","\"Finally, I have to attend lectures again...\"","He sighed and glanced toward the bed.","\"But damn, I’m already bored.\"","His gaze landed on Nancy, who was peacefully sleeping on the bed.","Noah stared at the cat for a few seconds.","\"You sleep all day. You’re so lucky. How good must your life be?\"","He couldn’t help but envy her carefree existence.","Unfortunately, unlike Nancy, he had responsibilities.","There was no point in complaining.","\"Sigh... let’s go. At least the instructor is Morgana. I can handle it.\"","With that, Noah left his dormitory room.","---","\"Is there something on my face?\"","Noah looked toward his left with a slightly confused expression.","Lyria was sitting beside him.","\"No... I mean, you never sat beside me before during class.\"","\"Well, there was a reason—\"","\"Because the two of us sit at the front, he used to avoid sitting beside us. But for some reason, he isn’t doing that anymore.\"","Arisha, sitting on Lyria’s other side, casually interrupted.","She spoke as though it were the most ordinary thing in the world.","\"She’s not wrong.\"","Noah couldn’t help but agree. There was no reason for him to hide it anymore.","\"It’s good to sit in the front. From now on, this is our fixed seat.\"","From Noah’s other side, Damien spoke.","\"Tch. I was hoping Arisha would sit here, but I guess there’s nothing I can do about it now.\"","\"Haha, you really don’t hide what you want.\"","Damien chuckled before patting Noah on the shoulder.","Noah glanced behind him.","A few seats away sat Ophelia.","The moment she noticed Noah’s gaze, she met his eyes and simply gave him a small nod.","Noah returned his attention to the front.","’Now I need to learn as much as possible about these side characters, especially the heroines.’","His expression became slightly thoughtful.","’Who knows? Maybe they have sad stories like Marina’s. I need to look into it.’","Just then, the classroom door opened.","A woman entered the room.","It was Morgana.","Her sky-blue hair was tied into a perfectly neat bun, while her amethyst eyes swept coldly across the entire classroom.","\"It appears everyone is present.\"","She walked toward the instructor’s desk.","\"Welcome back, everyone. The last month has been rather hectic. Monsters suddenly began emerging from an unknown location across various parts of the empire, including Novaris City itself.\"","Morgana placed one hand on the desk.","\"Fortunately, the situation has now been resolved. The academy also had to delay its reopening because of the incident.\"","Her cold gaze swept across the students once more.","\"But now, it is time to refocus on your studies and training.\"","She paused briefly.","\"I hope all of you are ready.\"","\"YES!!!\"","The students answered in unison.","\"Good.\"","Morgana nodded.","\"Now, let’s begin our first lecture.\"","---","Somewhere Far Away from Novaris Academy","In the largest city of the Aurellian Empire, a metropolis far grander than even Novaris City, stood the very heart of the empire.","Aurex Prime.","The magnificent city stretched across the horizon, filled with towering skyscrapers and beautiful modern buildings.","At the heart of the city, overlooking everything from atop a massive hill, stood the imperial palace.","It was enormous.","Its architecture combined modern grandeur with the majesty of an ancient royal fortress.","Inside the vast throne room, massive pillars stood along both sides, supporting the towering ceiling.","At the far end of the chamber was a grand staircase leading toward a majestic black-and-gold throne.","And upon that throne sat a man whose very presence carried the aura of a conqueror.","His dirty-blond hair was neatly combed, while a well-groomed beard framed his masculine features.","One arm rested casually on the throne’s armrest, while his other elbow supported his cheek.","His silver eyes stared forward with an indifferent expression.","He was one of the strongest human across the continent, Viserys Augustus, the Emperor of the strongest Empire, The Aurellian Empire.","A man with white hair stood beside his throne, reporting something to him. He was Baeon, an higher ranking minister in council and trusted person to Emepror.","\"Hmm... so the daughter of Narukami has returned.\"","Viserys’s expression remained indifferent.","\"That’s unexpected. But it is certainly interesting information to receive after I returned to my palace.\"","\"Your Majesty,\" Baeon continued respectfully, \"the monster hordes that had been emerging from the unknown location also stopped appearing and mysteriously perished on the very same day Lady Akari Narukami returned.\"","Viserys’s silver eyes narrowed slightly.","\"And here I have been traveling from place to place, searching for a solution to the situation.\"","His voice remained calm. \"Many others tried as well... yet no one succeeded.\"","He paused for a moment. \"Did you arrange a meeting with her?\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty. I have already sent a message to the Narukami family.\" He bowed his head.","\"Lady Akari has agreed to come here tomorrow to meet with His Imperial Majesty.\"","Viserys leaned back slightly against his throne. A faint glimmer appeared in his indifferent silver eyes."]},{"number":330,"title":"Chapter 330: New Dispute","paragraphs":["A week had passed since the academy reopened.","It was now the second week of the semester.","And today, something happened at the academy once again.","The cafeteria was unusually noisy. Students had gathered around something in the middle of the hall, creating a large crowd while excited voices echoed throughout the room.","Noah had just entered the cafeteria with Lyria and Arisha when the commotion immediately caught their attention.","The atmosphere felt strangely familiar.","Noah experienced a sudden sense of déjà vu.","It was almost identical to the atmosphere back when Damien had gotten into a fight with Edward.","\"What’s going on?\" Lyria wondered, looking toward the crowd.","\"Someone must be fighting,\" Arisha replied casually, as though there could hardly be any other explanation.","\"It must be Damien. He probably got into another fight.\"","\"Why do you think it must be him?\" Lyria asked.","\"Who else could it be? Don’t you remember? He got into a fight before, too.\"","\"Yes, but that doesn’t mean—\"","Before Lyria could finish her sentence, a voice from nearby interrupted them.","\"It’s Damien Ashworth! He got into an argument with someone!\"","A student nearby whispered excitedly to his friend before both of them hurried toward the crowd.","The three of them remained where they were for a moment.","\"Sigh... It’s really him,\" Lyria said helplessly. \"We should have joined the crowd earlier.\"","\"It’s Noah’s fault for not being able to finish that potion in time during alchemy class. And as if that wasn’t enough, he stopped both of us from going there with him.\"","Noah completely ignored Arisha’s complaint.","\"Putting that aside, let’s go and see who he’s arguing with this time.\"","The trio made their way through the crowd.","And when they finally reached the center, Noah’s expression changed.","Damien was standing there.","Emma stood behind him.","But opposite them was the last person Noah had expected to see.","A young man with dirty-blond hair and striking silver eyes stood proudly before them. He was handsome, sharp-featured, and roughly the same height as Noah.","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly.","’Prince Justinian Augustus.’","The second prince of the Aurellian Empire.","He was a second-year student at Novaris Academy.","’How the hell did Damien manage to get on his bad side?’","Justinian stood with an elegant, proud posture, his cold eyes fixed on Damien.","\"Damien, you should learn how to speak properly first. Surely, you understand who I am?\"","Damien looked slightly tense.","\"Your Highness, I didn’t mean it that way. I didn’t think you would take offense at what I said.\"","Emma immediately stepped forward and bowed.","\"Please forgive Damien Ashworth, Your Highness.\"","She kept her head lowered.","\"I apologize on his behalf.\"","Damien clenched his fists.","He clearly didn’t like seeing Emma apologize for something that was not her fault.","\"Emma, don’t apologize. You didn’t do anything wrong. And we are not at fault.\"","\"Then you should take responsibility for it, Damien.\"","Justinian took a step forward.","Several people standing behind him, his fellow second-year students and followers, remained silently behind him.","His gaze shifted toward Emma. \"And you are from the Hayes family... A count-ranked family, correct?\"","\"Yes, Your Grace.\"","Emma remained bowed, her voice slightly trembling as fear crept into her heart.","Damien was about to say something when another voice suddenly entered the conversation.","\"Oh my~ If it isn’t our esteemed Prince Justinian Augustus.\"","Everyone in the cafeteria turned toward the newcomer. And it was none other than Noah.","With a polite smile on his face, Noah walked toward Justinian. \"Greetings, Brother Justinian. It has been quite some time since last we crossed paths. I trust you hasn’t forgotten this humble man?\"","Justinian studied Noah for a moment. Then, a faint smirk appeared on his face.","\"Of course I remember you. How could I possibly forget the exiled son of House Eldritch, whose notorious habits were once the talk of noble circles?\"","Damien and Emma looked at Noah in surprise.","Noah, however, showed no reaction to the remark. His smile remained perfectly intact.","He walked forward and positioned himself between Damien and Justinian. \"It is indeed an honor that Your Highness still remembers me.\"","Noah glanced toward Damien before returning his attention to Justinian. \"Yet, judging by the present circumstances, it would seem that my friend has committed some offense against your highness. Though I know not the nature of his transgression, I humbly ask that Your Highness overlook his mistake.\"","Justinian let out a quiet chuckle. \"Oh, Noah. When did I ever say that I intended to punish him?\"","He tilted his head slightly. \"Why do you assume such a thing? Am I truly so fearsome in your eyes?\"","Noah maintained his polite smile. But internally, he was cursing. ’Of course you bastard. I know exactly what kind of piece of shit you are.’","As the son of a duke, Noah had naturally known the second prince since childhood. Justinian possessed everything expected of an imperial prince.","He was handsome, charming, elegant, and dignified. But Noah knew that those qualities were merely a mask.","Behind that refined appearance was a petty, arrogant, and selfish man who looked down upon commoners and rarely tolerated anything that displeased him.","Noah still didn’t know what Damien had said that had offended him.","Justinian’s expression showed no obvious anger. He was even smiling.","Yet Noah knew better. Something was wrong.","’Dammit. We never even crossed paths during the first semester. So why now?’","During the first semester, most of the conflicts had involved first-year students. But now that the second semester had begun,","Noah realized that students from the upper years might become involved as well. And if Justinian was now taking an interest in Damien.","’This is going to bring even more trouble into his life.’","\"Of course not, Your Highness.\" Noah’s smile never faltered.","\"Everyone knows that you to be a most benevolent and generous prince.\"","Justinian’s eyes narrowed slightly at the flattery, though his smile remained.","Noah then turned toward Damien. \"Damien, you should bow and offer them apology. Do not allow others to become entangled in your mistake, nor let another speak on your behalf. If you has earn, then face it by yourself.\"","Damien clenched his fist again. He clearly wasn’t pleased by Noah’s words.","But he glanced around. The crowd had grown considerably larger, and even Emma had bowed before the prince to apologize on his behalf.","Noah’s words were reasonable. After a brief hesitation, Damien finally relented.","He stepped forward and bowed to Justinian. \"I apologize for my mistake. I shouldn’t have said those words.\"","Justinian stared at Damien for a moment.","Then his expression softened into a faint smile.","\"See? It was not so difficult, was it?\" He spoke with the calm confidence of a senior instructing a junior.","\"As thy senior, I merely wished to teach the importance of accepting responsibility for one’s mistakes.\"","His gaze lingered on Damien. \"And you has done well. After all, you are the first-ranked student among the first years, Damien Ashworth.\"","He then looked around the cafeteria. \"And why have all of are gathered here?\"","His tone became slightly amused. \"This is a cafeteria, is it not? You all to be enjoying the meal rather than standing about and watching a trivial dispute.\"","The students immediately began dispersing.","One by one, the crowd returned to their tables, and within moments, the commotion that had filled the cafeteria began to fade.","Just as the situation seemed to be over, however, Justinian’s gaze wandered across the room.","His silver eyes suddenly stopped. They landed on Lyria. For a brief moment, his eyes widened ever so slightly.","Then, slowly his smile grew a little wider."]},{"number":331,"title":"Chapter 331: We are close...","paragraphs":["\"Oh my, if it isn’t Lady Lyria Sunweave.\" Justinian’s expression brightened as he approached, a charming smile spreading across his face.","Lyria, who was standing beside Arisha, immediately straightened and gave him a light bow. \"Greetings, Your Highness.\"","Arisha followed her lead and bowed as well. \"Greetings, Your Highness.\"","\"There is no need for such formalities. We are within the academy, after all. You may simply address me as Senior.\"","His tone was polite and friendly. And this time it looked genuine, unlike how it felt false mask while talking with Noah and Damien.","Both girls straightened at his words.","\"It’s been a while, Senior,\" Lyria said respectfully. \"And please don’t call me ’Lady’ while we’re here. I’m merely a student and your junior.\"","At her words, Justinian’s smile widened slightly. \"Very well, Junior Lyria.\"","His silver eyes then shifted toward Arisha, taking in her equally striking appearance. \"And you?\"","\"Arisha Willow.\"","\"Oh. Junior Arisha.\"","Noah watched the exchange from the side, his eyebrow twitching slightly.","’Is this bastard interested in Lyria or something?I didn’t like it.’","His eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","’Let’s test it.’ Without giving anyone time to react, Noah stepped forward and moved beside Lyria.","\"It appears you know Lyria quite well, Senior.\"","Before anyone could question what he was doing, Noah casually placed an arm around Lyria’s shoulders and gently pulled her toward him.","Her soft side of big chest pressed against his side. Lyria let out a small gasp. \"No-Noah?!\"","She looked at him in surprise, her pink eyes widening as a warm blush quickly spread across her cheeks.","\"What are you doing?\"","Noah calmly met her gaze. His fingers gave her shoulder a gentle squeeze, almost as if reassuring her.","His expression remained perfectly calm. His eyes seemed to tell her without words.","As if he was trying to say, ’Just go along with it.’","Lyria stared at him for a moment, confused and flustered.","Arisha, meanwhile, raised a single eyebrow. Damien and Emma looked equally stunned watching from side, they were also just few steps away.","Even several students who had been about to leave stopped in their tracks and turned around to watch.","But among all of them, one reaction immediately caught Noah’s attention.","Justinian’s expression had turned icy cold. \"What is the meaning of this, Noah?\"","His previously charming smile had vanished. \"Touching Junior Lyria in such a manner is most inappropriate. You cannot simply—\"","\"Your Highness—\" Noah paused. \"Ah, I mean, Senior.\"","He smiled politely. \"I’m quite close with Lyria, and she doesn’t mind it.\"","Noah looked down at Lyria. \"Right, Lyria? Or are you angry?\"","\"I-I mean...\" Lyria’s face became even redder. \"I’m mean I’m certainly not angry... but we’re in public, so this is...\"","\"Come on, why worry about what others think?\" Noah smiled casually. \"We’re close, aren’t we? I don’t think we need to hide it.\"","Justinian’s jaw tightened. His teeth clenched slightly, though he quickly concealed his reaction. His gaze shifted toward Lyria.","Her face was flushed with embarrassment, her expression shy and flustered. Clearly, he wasn’t enjoying what he was seeing.","And Noah noticed. ’This guy really does have something for Lyria. Dammit! My innocent saint is in danger!’","Noah’s expression remained perfectly composed despite the alarm bells going off inside his head.","Justinian took a slow breath, seemingly forcing himself to calm down.","He then looked back at Noah. \"I was not aware... that the two of you were like this.\"","His smile returned, though it looked somewhat forced. \"Well, regardless, I shall take my leave. It was a pleasure meeting you all.\"","With that, Justinian turned around and began walking away.","Noah’s eyes widened. ’Wait!’","\"Senior—\"","\"Noah!\" Before he could call after him, Damien suddenly rushed over.","Emma followed closely behind. \"What the hell was that?! When did this happen?\"","Noah glanced at Damien and clicked his tongue internally. ’Not right now.’","By the time he looked back, Justinian was already walking away with his followers, leaving them behind.","’Well...’","Noah sighed. ’It’s not like that me clearing things will change anything.’","Still, he couldn’t deny one thing. ’But damn that expression on his face was pretty amusing. I liked it.’","\"Noah, I’m asking you something!\"","Damien’s voice brought him back to reality.","Noah looked at him and sighed. \"Whatever you’re thinking, it’s not like that between me and Lyria.\"","\"Then why did you act like that?\" Emma asked in confusion. Damien nodded, clearly having the same question.","\"And could you release the poor girl from your clutches?\" Arisha pointed toward Lyria.","Only then did Noah realize something. He was still holding Lyria against him. He immediately released her and stepped away.","\"Ahem. Sorry about that Lyria.\"","He coughed lightly, pretending nothing unusual had happened. \"I only did that because I wanted to understand something.\"","\"Understand what?\" Lyria asked, still looking slightly flustered.","She didn’t seem angry, though. \"I didn’t push you away because I knew you must have had a reason for doing that.\"","Noah nodded. \"I did.\"","He glanced toward where Justinian had disappeared. \"I’ll explain everything while we eat lunch.\"","Just then, a loud voice echoed across the cafeteria.","\"Hello, everyone! What’s up? Why are you guys just standing around here? Did something happen?\"","Leonard and Kaelan had just entered the cafeteria and were making their way toward the group. Leonard looked around at everyone’s expressions.","Noah glanced at them. \"Well...\"","A faint smile appeared on his face. \"You two certainly missed something amazing.\" he shook his head.","Then he looked at Damien. \"Also, Damien, I would like to understand what you did to make the prince angry.\"","Damien frowned but nodded. \"I didn’t do anything wrong. That man just got offended over something so small. Let’s find a table. I’ll tell you all about it.\"","And so, the group once again carried their lunches over to a table and sat down.","Whatever Damien was about to tell them, this conversation might turn out to be either very interesting or maybe dangerous."]},{"number":332,"title":"Chapter 332: About Prince Justinian","paragraphs":["\"So, you mean...\" Noah paused, recounting everything Damien had told him. \"Let me get this straight. You were simply walking when he bumped into your shoulder. Then you told him, ’Watch where you’re going, bro, or you might get hurt.’\"","\"Yes,\" Damien replied, sitting across from Noah. \"But I said it in a friendly tone. I was even smiling.\"","\"Huh...\" Noah nodded slowly. \"And the prince didn’t like your friendly tone, so he told you that wasn’t how you should speak to him and warned you to watch your tone.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"And then you said, ’What’s wrong with my tone, brother? I only told you to be more careful next time. If you were offended, then I’m sorry. But there’s no need to get angry over something so small.’\"","\"Yup.\"","\"And that made him even angrier.\" Noah sighed and shook his head.","\"What a shitty way to get on the bad side of a prince. Well, if you were a beautiful girl, you might have been forgiven more easily.\"","Damien’s lips twitched. \"Tch. I didn’t even know he was a prince at first. It took me a while to recognize him. If I’d known from the beginning, I would’ve apologized right away.\"","\"No, you wouldn’t have.\"","Noah gave him a knowing look. \"I know you. You would’ve tried to escalate the situation even further because you thought you weren’t in the wrong.\"","Damien immediately fell silent.","Because Noah was right.","\"Well, thanks to Noah, we were able to calm the situation down,\" Emma said from Damien’s left.","Noah looked at her in mild surprise.","She had actually said something good about him.","\"True. Thanks, Noah,\" Damien added.","\"It’s fine.\"","\"Shit! I missed the drama!\" Leonard’s stunned voice suddenly came from beside them.","The group had chosen a table in one of the quieter corners of the cafeteria, away from the main crowd. With all of them sitting close together, the surrounding noise made it difficult for anyone nearby to hear their conversation.","Leonard had taken the seat beside Arisha, while Arisha sat to Noah’s right.","\"It was a pretty serious situation, to be honest,\" Leonard continued. \"If Damien had ended up on the bad side of Prince Justinian...\"","\"Why?\" Arisha asked.","\"Well, since you’re not from a noble family, you might not know this.\"","Leonard lowered his voice. \"Prince Justinian is a two-faced man. He acts kind and polite toward everyone, but he’s extremely petty, arrogant, prideful, and... well, let’s just say he’s not someone you want as an enemy.\"","He glanced around before continuing. \"Most nobles around our age, as well as those in his generation, know what he’s really like. We just pretend we don’t.\"","\"Are you sure?\" Arisha asked again, her expression skeptical.","\"Yes.\"","Before Leonard could elaborate, Lyria spoke.","\"He’s right. I remember something from a few years ago.\"","Everyone turned toward her.","\"During a banquet held by the imperial family for the First Prince’s birthday, a young man from a count’s family made a joke while speaking with Justinian.\"","Lyria’s expression became thoughtful.","\"He said something about hoping Justinian would become more like his older brother, the First Prince. I was there that night, so I remember it clearly.\"","She glanced around the table. \"Kaelan, Noah, and even Leonard were there as well.\"","\"And what happened afterward?\" Damien asked curiously.","\"Justinian simply laughed it off at the time,\" Kaelan answered.","\"But a few weeks later, we heard that the same young man had been accused of stealing a brooch belonging to Prince Justinian—a brooch that had been given to him by his mother.\"","Leonard snorted. \"It was obviously fabricated. We all knew it.\"","\"Damn...\" Damien’s expression changed. \"Isn’t that going too far?\"","\"What happened to the guy?\" Arisha asked.","\"Nothing serious, apparently,\" Noah answered.","He leaned back slightly.","\"According to what I heard, he eventually begged Justinian for forgiveness and even knelt before him. Justinian supposedly forgave him afterward, and that young man eventually became one of his followers.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"And he was standing behind Justinian earlier.\"","Damien swallowed. \"That’s dangerous.\"","He paused. \"I really am lucky.\"","\"True,\" Arisha muttered.","Leonard shrugged. \"Though you probably would’ve only had to deal with some bullying from his followers.\"","He paused. \"Or something worse. I honestly have no idea.\"","Damien’s expression stiffened. \"Please don’t say things like that so casually.\"","Everyone ignored him.","Arisha turned her attention toward Noah. \"Now tell us why you did that to Lyria.\"","Noah shrugged. \"I just had a feeling...\" He glanced around the table before lowering his voice. \"I thought Justinian might be interested in Lyria.\"","Everyone became slightly more attentive.","\"So I wanted to confirm it.\" Noah continued.","\"I acted as though Lyria and I were extremely close. And when I did that, his expression immediately changed. He was clearly annoyed and angry.\"","He tapped his fingers lightly against the table. \"That pretty much confirmed my suspicion that he might actually have feelings for her.\"","Silence fell around the table.","Even Lyria blinked in surprise.","\"Then... it might really be true.\"","Noah looked at her. \"You had doubts too? Has he approached you before?\"","\"Yes...\"","Lyria nodded. \"He spoke to me a few times during the first semester, but it was mostly just polite greetings.\"","She sighed softly. \"I never thought much of it.\"","Emma frowned. \"Noah... doesn’t that put you on the bad side of the prince?\"","Noah pressed his lips into a thin line. \"Yeah...\"","He rubbed the back of his neck. \"I mean, the way I was holding Lyria and the way she was blushing probably made us look like a couple.\"","He glanced at Lyria. \"It looked like I was openly accepting the relationship while she was just too shy to admit it.\"","Lyria’s cheeks immediately turned bright red.","Noah noticed her reaction and awkwardly looked away.","Arisha also waited for his answer.","After a moment, Noah simply shrugged.","\"Whatever. I can clear up the misunderstanding whenever I want. It’s not a big problem.\"","\"Hmm...\" Kaelan folded his arms. \"But a lot of students saw you. There are bound to be rumors about the two of you.\"","\"Re-really?\" Lyria’s pink eyes widened. \"Rumors?\"","Noah casually waved his hand. \"Who cares? They’re just rumors.\"","\"Then when are you going to clear things up with the prince?\" Arisha asked, resting her chin against her hand.","\"Not for now.\"","A small smirk appeared on Noah’s face.","\"W-what? Why not?\" Lyria asked, visibly flustered.","\"Well, let him believe it for now.\"","Noah leaned back in his chair. \"Maybe he’ll lose interest in you and give up.\"","Leonard shook his head. \"He doesn’t look like the type of person who gives up easily.\"","\"If that happens, I’ll clear things up.\" Noah paused. \"Or maybe I won’t.\"","He smiled mischievously. \"Either way, we should protect my—\" He stopped himself. \"I mean... our cute Lyria.\"","Lyria’s entire face flushed with warmth.","\"U-Ugh...\"","She lowered her head, unable to look at anyone.","Arisha simply shook her head. \"Sure. We should.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement before returning to their lunch.","Their conversation gradually shifted to other topics as they continued eating.","None of them noticed that, from another corner of the cafeteria, someone had been quietly watching their table the entire time."]},{"number":333,"title":"Chapter 333: Puppet of the Frost Dragon","paragraphs":["Noah stood alone in one corner of the training ground.","The reason was simple. He wanted to test his newly acquired ability.","[Puppet of the Frost Dragon]","Considering everything he had gone through, the rewards he had received had honestly felt rather underwhelming.","At least, they had seemed that way to his current self. But there was only one way to know whether the ability was truly disappointing.","Test it and judge it.","Noah cracked his fingers one after another, then stretched his arms and rolled his shoulders.","\"Alright. Let’s see what you’ve got.\"","He raised one hand and slowly began channeling his mana. The moment he activated the ability, the atmosphere around him changed.","The temperature dropped sharply.","A thin layer of frost immediately spread across the ground beneath his feet, while countless fragments of ice began materializing out of thin air. They were beautiful, almost like translucent crystals carved from pure winter, shimmering faintly beneath the morning light.","More and more ice gathered around Noah.","The fragments began circling his body, slowly at first, before picking up speed. His mana started draining rapidly.","’So it consumes quite a lot of mana just to activate...’","The swirling ice suddenly intensified.","A miniature blizzard erupted around Noah, its freezing winds whipping against his clothes and sending countless snowflakes and ice particles spiraling through the air.","Whoosh!","The blizzard shot forward.","It continued expanding as it moved, growing larger and larger while the surrounding wind accelerated. The swirling mass of frost soon became several times larger than Noah himself.","And then, within the center of the raging blizzard.","Something began to form.","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","’It’s forming.’","At first, four enormous claws made of ice emerged from within the storm.","The claws slowly transformed into powerful legs. From there, the structure continued growing.","A massive body took shape, followed by a long, thick tail that stretched behind it. Then came the neck, rising higher and higher, until finally a dragon’s head emerged.","Two sharp horns formed above its skull. One after another, layers of crystalline scales spread across its entire body, each one looking as though it had been carved from the purest ice.","The blizzard gradually weakened.","The violent winds slowed. Snow and frost drifted harmlessly through the air before settling onto the ground.","And finally, the creature was revealed, it was a dragon.","It was nowhere near the size of Akari’s true dragon form, of course. Compared to that monstrous scale, this creature was practically tiny.","But that did not mean it was small. From the tip of its snout to the end of its tail, the Frost Dragon was approximately ten meters long.","Its massive wings unfolded from its back.","Each wing stretched roughly ten meters from one end to the other, their surfaces composed entirely of beautiful translucent ice.","It was more than large enough for Noah to sit comfortably on its back and fly.","Noah stared at the creature in fascination. Then he noticed something strange.","’Wait...’","The dragon was moving. Not because Noah had commanded it.","It was moving on its own. Noah could somehow feel a connection between them, a strange, almost instinctive bond.","He could sense its presence as clearly as he could sense his own mana. A smile slowly appeared on his face.","He didn’t say anything. Instead, he simply looked at the Frost Dragon.","’Look at me.’","The moment the thought entered his mind.","The dragon turned its enormous head. Its glacier-like eyes focused directly on Noah. They were cold and emotionless, almost devoid of any natural emotion. Yet there was no hostility in them.","There was only obedience.","Noah’s smile widened. \"So you really can understand me...\"","He walked toward the dragon. As he approached, the Frost Dragon lowered its massive head toward him, almost as though it were willingly offering itself.","Noah reached out and placed his hand against its head. The surface was freezing cold.","Yet the cold did not hurt him. Instead, the ice seemed to welcome his touch.","Noah gently patted its head. \"Hah...\"","He glanced at his remaining mana and sighed. \"That took roughly one-fourth of my mana just to create you.\"","He looked back at the Frost Dragon.","\"And your strength...\"","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly as he sensed its power.","\"It should be around the same level as my current core rank.\"","A huge grin spread across his face.","’This is actually amazing. When I wiill reach mythical rank then I can create a mythical rank frost dragon!!’","For someone who had expected the ability to be disappointing, Noah was now thoroughly impressed.","Unfortunately his excitement didn’t last very long.","\"A dragon?!\"","\"That’s a real dragon!\"","Noah froze. He slowly turned toward the source of the voices.","A few meters away, several students had been training. Some had stopped what they were doing and were now staring at the Frost Dragon with expressions of complete shock.","Others had gathered around them, pointing at the enormous creature.","Noah blinked.","’Hmm...’","He turned his attention back toward his newly created puppet.","An idea suddenly came to him. Noah raised his right arm, and decided to perform something that he always wanted to do.","\"Frosty!\"","The dragon’s glacier-colored eyes shifted toward him.","Noah pointed forward. \"Flame Thrower!\"","He did a command like how those trainers from Pokemoon anime used to do. But what came out of his mouth was most common attack in that anime by Charlizaard, forgetting his puppet is ice user.","So there was absolute silence after her spoke that.","Noah remained frozen in place. The students stared at him as if he had suddenly lost his mind.","The Frost Dragon tilted its head slightly. It looked at Noah. Then it looked at the students. Then it opened its enormous jaws.","Noah’s expression changed.","\"Well, I mean—frost—\"","BOOOOM!","A brilliant blue-white stream of freezing flames erupted from the dragon’s mouth. It shot directly toward the students.","\"The hell?! RUN!\"","\"You madman!\"","\"NOAH!\"","The students scattered in every direction. The blue frost-fire crashed into the ground with a thunderous roar.","CRACK!","A layer of ice instantly spread across everything the flames touched. The ground froze solid.","Patches of frost rapidly expanded outward, covering the training area in a beautiful but terrifying layer of blue-white ice.","Fortunately, there had been no intention to actually harm anyone, and the students had managed to escape the attack.","Noah stared at the frozen ground. His eyes sparkled.","’This...’ His gaze slowly shifted toward the Frost Dragon. ’This thing is amazing!’","He couldn’t help but feel excited. Not only could it fight independently, but it could apparently interpret his commands as well.","Although perhaps he should work on his naming skills.","Noah’s expression became thoughtful.","’ So the dragon was created using one-fourth of my mana...’","He rubbed his chin.","’That means it has roughly that much mana stored within its body.’","His eyes narrowed as he continued analyzing the ability.","’And if it runs out of mana, I’ll have to supply it with more mana to maintain its physical form and also to use magic.’","That explained the connection he could feel between them.","The Frost Dragon wasn’t simply a summoned creature. It was a puppet created from Noah’s own mana.","As long as he continued supplying it with mana, the Frost Dragon could remain active.","The dragon slowly lowered its head before standing proudly, its massive wings folding against its body.","Noah walked over and gave one of its enormous legs a satisfied pat.","\"Good job.\"","The Frost Dragon remained perfectly still.","Noah nodded approvingly. ’I really wish I had a cool frost-fire attack like that too.’","He looked at the frozen training ground. Then at the Frost Dragon. Then back at the frozen ground.","\"...Maybe I should learn one if possible... but how?\""]},{"number":334,"title":"Chapter 334: First Prince Justinian, and now...","paragraphs":["The days passed faster than Noah expected.","He kept wondering when the next incident would occur, yet for some reason, everything had been far too peaceful.","Nearly three weeks had passed since the academy reopened, and so far, Noah had done little more than train and practice.","And that, ironically, was beginning to make him nervous.","Noah sat on a bench at the edge of the training ground, resting his back against it as he stared at the evening sky.","He let out a long sigh.","He wanted to explore another dungeon and experience something exciting, but after what he had gone through inside the labyrinth with Damien, a part of him also wanted to stay as far away from dungeons as possible.","’There has to be something troublesome going on.’","His instincts refused to believe that things could remain this peaceful for long.","’Even Prince Justinian hasn’t done anything against Damien or me.’","Noah narrowed his eyes slightly.","’Though I’ve seen him a few times since then. He didn’t say anything, but the hostility in his eyes was obvious.’","Fortunately, nothing had happened yet. After sitting there for a while longer, Noah finally decided to return to his dormitory.","It was already evening. He stood up from the bench and made his way through the academy’s corridors.","Even at this hour, the halls remained lively.","Students walked around in groups, chatting with their friends after finishing their daily training and classes. Some were discussing their lessons, while others were simply enjoying their free time.","Then Noah noticed something else.","A few pairs of students men and women were walking together while holding hands.","Their faces were slightly flushed, and their expressions were filled with the unmistakable embarrassment of young couples enjoying their time together.","Noah clicked his tongue.","Tch.","’They’re enjoying romance while I’m over here worrying about what kind of disaster is going to fall on my head next.’","He couldn’t help but feel bitter about his life.","Even the one woman who had managed to make his heart genuinely beat faster had been separated from him before he could fall head overs for her.","Noah sighed. ’Maybe I already am...’","He paused. Then another thought suddenly entered his mind.","’Hmm... Since I’m living in a new world where having multiple wives isn’t exactly unusual... should I try it?’","His imagination began running wild.","’Become incredibly strong, make a fortune, marry several beautiful women, have lots of children, and then watch them grow up and fight over my property and legacy—’","Noah’s expression stiffened. ’...What the hell am I thinking?’","That train of thought had gone in a very strange direction. He definitely shouldn’t be fantasizing about enjoying the sight of his own children fighting over his wealth.","Though the idea of having multiple wives and a large family wasn’t exactly unpleasant.","Noah rubbed his chin.","’Maybe I should create my own clan someday, after I survive all the dangers surrounding me.’","A faint smile appeared on his face.","’ Well, only if there’s no way for me to return to my original world . ’","The thought immediately made that smile disappear. A bitter feeling settled in his chest as he look down at floor.","He had once been determined to find a way back home. But after spending so much time living as Noah Eldritch, things had gradually changed.","He had grown accustomed to this world, to his new identity, to his family, friends, to the people he had met.","Even his memories of his former life no longer felt as vivid as they once had.","’I can’t let that happen.’ He clenched his fist slightly. ’I can’t let myself forget my original life completely.’","Thud!","Something suddenly bumped into his shoulder.","Noah’s thoughts were interrupted. \"I’m sorry! I wasn’t looking where I was going.\"","He instinctively raised a hand to apologize as well. But the moment he looked at the person in front of him and he froze.","A bead of sweat slowly rolled down his forehead. He couldn’t tell whether it was because of the hours of training he had endured earlier.","Or because of the person standing before him.","’Why?’","His expression twitched. ’First Prince Justinian, and now...’","Standing before him was a beautiful woman with long, maroon-colored hair cascading down her back.","Her silver eyes were cold and sharp.","She looked at Noah with an indifferent expression, as though he were nothing more than an insignificant passerby.","\"Noah Eldritch.\"","Her voice was calm. \"You should look where you are going. Walking while staring at the ground is a rather bad habit.\"","Noah’s mouth twitched. He immediately recognized her.","\"Your Highness—\"","\"No need to address me like that.\"","She interrupted him without hesitation.","Noah quickly adjusted his attitude. \"Huh... Senior Viserra, then. It is a pleasure to meet you, and I apologize for my mistake.\"","’Shit.’","His expression remained polite, but his thoughts were anything but.","’Another dangerous person. First Prince Justinian, and now her? Why am I meeting all these troublesome people during this semester?’","Noah had only seen her once during his first semester, and even then, it had been from a distance. But he knew exactly who she was.","Viserra Augustus.","The First Princess of the Aurellian Empire. A third-year student at Novaris Academy.","If Justinian was a two-faced man who presented himself as kind and courteous while hiding his arrogant and petty nature beneath that mask, Viserra was different.","She didn’t rely on the same sort of facade.","According to what Noah’s elder brother had told him two years ago, Viserra was far more cunning and manipulative.","She was the kind of woman who would use people however she pleased if doing so brought her closer to whatever goal she had set for herself.","And despite being only twenty-two years old, she possessed an exceptionally sharp mind.","Noah had never interacted with her personally before. So he had no idea why she had suddenly approached him now.","Viserra studied him silently for several seconds.","Her silver eyes narrowed slightly, as though she were examining something hidden beneath his appearance.","A faint, amused smile appeared on her lips.","\"Noah Eldritch...\" She tilted her head slightly. \"You have changed quite a bit since the last time I saw you.\"","Noah maintained his polite expression. \"People change. The time I spent after being exiled from my family taught me many things. Most of them, I had to learn on my own.\"","Viserra’s smile deepened slightly.","For a moment, she said nothing. Her gaze continued to linger on him, as though she were assessing him from head to toe.","Then she finally spoke. \"I suppose it was fortunate that I met you today.\"","\"Hmm?\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"Pardon?\"","Viserra turned around. \"I wanted to speak with you.\"","She began walking down the corridor without waiting for a response. \"Follow me.\"","Noah remained standing there for a moment. He stared at her back.","’What does she want from me?’ His instincts were screaming that following her was probably a terrible idea.","Unfortunately, ignoring the First Princess of the Aurellian Empire probably wasn’t a particularly wise option either.","---","She led Noah to a secluded corridor of the academy.","Noah looked around and saw that no one else was there.","She stopped near an open window and leaned against it. The soft evening breeze made her hair sway gently.","As someone who had always appreciated beautiful women, Noah couldn’t deny that the princess was beautiful. However, he didn’t feel the same attraction toward her that he felt toward Arisha, Lyria, or Akira.","\"So, Noah.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"A few weeks ago... my brother Justinian had a heated moment with... one of your classmates named Damien, am I right?\"","\"Yes, that’s right...\"","\"Hmm. But it was resolved... You stepped in, and everything went well... but...\"","Her silver eyes stared directly at him.","\"Never would I have expected you to be in a relationship with Lyria of Sunweave. You do know what would happen if word reached her father... or perhaps it already has...\"","Noah’s lips twitched.","To be honest, all he knew about Lyria’s father was that he was a devoted follower of the Sun God and supposedly a kind-hearted man.","But perhaps that wasn’t the whole story.","’I guess this might become more problematic than I initially expected... but well not like I accepted or reveal with my mouth that we are actually in relationship. This is what people think...’","---","[A/N: Hello, guys! I know you must be cursing me and wondering, \"Why is this bastard author only uploading one Chapter again?\"","Well, I’m focusing more on the story right now, especially the big families and the important characters from them. For example, I’ve just introduced two new characters, so I want to take my time and develop things carefully instead of rushing through them.","Also, guys, the novel did pretty badly last month. We didn’t get many new readers, so please support the novel by sending some gifts. I know it’s shameless of me to ask, but maybe, just maybe, I’ll make one reader’s wish come true for the MC if they send a Super Gift.","Just pray that the request isn’t too weird or crazy!]"]},{"number":335,"title":"Chapter 335: You have my support","paragraphs":["Now standing beside Viserra, Noah quietly wondered what he should say next.","’Should I tell her there’s nothing between Lyria and me and clear up the misunderstanding?’","Before he could decide, Viserra broke the silence. \"To be honest, I have nothing to do with the matter. It is your life, after all. Though it’s very bad situation for a exiled son and a daughter of another duke to be in relationship.\"","She paused for a moment before continuing. \"And you should know that my brother seems to have some interest in Lyria Sunweave.\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","’Wait...Is she worried for her brother and want me to leave Lyria? When did she start caring about her brother’s love life?’","As far as he remembered, Viserra and Justinian were half-siblings born to different mothers. They were members of the same imperial family, but they had never appeared particularly close.","’Something feels strange about this.’","Rather than wait for her to explain further, Noah decided to speak first. \"So, Senior... are you asking me to stay away from Lyria?\"","Viserra raised an eyebrow. Then a soft chuckle escaped her lips. \"What? Why would I want that? I am not some evil woman.\"","A smile slowly bloomed across her face. \"Quite the opposite. I am telling you not to fear my brother.\"","Her silver eyes narrowed slightly with amusement. \"You have my support. Do not leave her.\"","Noah blinked.","’Yep. This is how it should be. She doesn’t like her brother. She definitely hate him.’","In fact, she seemed almost delighted by the fact that the woman Justinian had taken an interest in already had someone close to her, maybe have lover.","Noah deliberately widened his eyes. \"You... you really mean that?\"","\"Of course.\"","Viserra’s smile remained. \"Do you doubt the word of a member of the imperial family?\"","\"Of course not.\" Noah immediately bowed. \"I am deeply grateful that you are willing to support me.\"","But he was also confused . ’ Should I pretend that Lyria and I are already in a relationship? No...’","That would be too risky. There was no need to create another unnecessary complication, especially with someone as cunning as Viserra.","’I’ll tell her a half-truth instead. I don’t want to create unnecessary trouble with the princess either.’","Noah straightened his posture.","\"But, Senior...\"","\"Yes?\"","\"There has been a misunderstanding between Lyria and me... and, well, among the students.\"","Viserra frowned slightly. \"What misunderstanding?\"","\"The truth is...\" Noah hesitated. He lowered his gaze, as though struggling to find the right words. \"Lyria and I are not in a relationship.\"","Silence.","Viserra’s expression froze. She slowly uncrossed her arms. Then she looked directly at Noah. \"You two are not in a relationship?\"","\"Yes.\" He replied.","Her eyes narrowed. \"Then how could you act so intimately with her? You touched her and held her in front of everyone.\"","Her voice had become colder. The amusement and delight that had been present only moments ago disappeared almost instantly.","\"There was a reason.\"","\"Then explain.\" She ask for explanation.","Noah took a small breath. \"You see, I am very close to Lyria, but only as a friend. She trusts me, and because of that, she doesn’t mind normal physical contact between us.\"","He paused. \"But...\"","Noah’s expression became slightly embarrassed. \"I... I actually love her.\"","As he said those words, he deliberately avoided Viserra’s eyes. A faint flush appeared on his cheeks.","Viserra stared at him. The coldness in her silver eyes slowly disappeared. \"You love her...\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah nodded. \"That day, His Highness Prince Justinian was showing a great deal of interest in Lyria.\"","He lowered his head slightly. \"And, well...\"","His voice became quieter. \"I became jealous.\"","Viserra’s eyebrows rose.","\"So I intervened. That’s why I held her like that.\"","\"Oh...\"","Her expression softened. \"So that’s what happened.\"","\"Yes.\"","Noah gave an awkward smile.","\"I... I’ve been trying to express my feelings to Lyria through my actions. I think she has already noticed how I feel, but she hasn’t given me an answer yet. And that day she didn’t push me away.\"","He lowered his gaze again. \"It seems she is confused about her own feelings as well.\"","Viserra fell silent. She crossed her arms once again and began thinking deeply about what Noah had just told her.","Meanwhile, Noah maintained the expression of a young man desperately trying to win the heart of the woman he loved.","Inside, however, ’Good. Good. This should be enough. I was worried she might ask me to stay close with Lyria, don’t hide it or do something that could provoke Justinian even further. But with this explanation, there shouldn’t be any problem. At least... I hope so.’","After several seconds, Viserra finally spoke. \"Hmm...\"","A faint smile returned to her lips. \"Interesting.\"","She looked at Noah. \"Regardless, you have my support. Do not stop pursuing the girl you love simply because of Justinian. And you have changed a lot, also you are at second rank in first year. That’s amazing achievement.\"","Noah immediately nodded. \"Yes, Senior. I won’t. And thanks for compliment.\"","A polite smile appeared on his face. ’It worked.’","Noah inwardly breathed a sigh of relief. ’’I guess that’s all she wanted to talk about.’","He had expected the First Princess to summon him for something important or perhaps some serious political matter. And Noah was bad at politics, that’s for sure.","Instead, they had spent their time discussing his supposed relationship with Lyria.","’What a strange conversation.’","Noah was about to say something when Viserra suddenly spoke again.","\"By the way...\" She smiled. \"There is something else I wanted to ask you.\"","Noah paused.","\"Yes?\"","\"Tell me about Damien Ashworth.\"","Viserra’s smile remained as she looked directly at him. \"Your friend and classmate.\"","Noah’s expression remained calm, but his eyes narrowed slightly.","\"I already know about him. After all, he holds the first rank among the first-year students.\"","She paused briefly. \"But I want to know more about him from someone who is actually close to him.\"","Noah sighed inwardly. ’Well, well, well... Here it comes. The protagonist is attracting attention from another important character for absolutely no reason.’","He resisted the urge to sigh aloud. \"Of course.\"","Noah smiled politely. \"What would you like to know about him?\""]},{"number":336,"title":"Chapter 336: He definitely knows","paragraphs":["Another day.","Noah yawned as he walked toward his classroom, his hands casually tucked into his pockets. Just yesterday, he had ended up having a rather unexpected conversation with Viserra Augustus.","And what could he say about it? The conversation had started with Lyria and the misunderstanding surrounding their relationship.","Somehow, it had ended with Viserra asking him several questions about Damien. She hadn’t asked too many, but the questions themselves had been important.","For example, she had asked about the labyrinth incident, the very incident during which Noah had disappeared.","Of course, Noah hadn’t told her the whole truth.","From the way Viserra had reacted, Noah was fairly certain she hadn’t completely believed his explanation either.","She had also asked whether Damien was currently in a relationship, whether he liked anyone, what kind of personality he had, and even what sort of things he enjoyed.","At the time, Noah had simply answered carefully. But afterward, one question had remained stuck in his mind.","’Does she have a crush on Damien?’ Noah shook his head. ’No. That’s not possible.’","Viserra was the First Princess of the empire.","Damien was a commoner who had risen to become the top-ranked first-year student. There were certainly worse possibilities, but Noah couldn’t imagine that being the reason.","Besides, Viserra had explicitly told him that he could tell Damien about her questions if he wanted.","’Then there has to be another reason.’","Noah frowned slightly.","’ What could she possibly want with Damien?’","He hadn’t been able to figure it out.","\"NOAH!\"","A loud voice suddenly broke through his thoughts. Noah blinked and turned around.","Damien was approaching him with his usual enormous grin. The moment he caught up, Damien raised a hand.","\"Wassup, man?\"","\"Nothing much.\"","Noah glanced at him. \"You’re early today.\"","Damien looked offended. \"I’m early every day.\"","\"Yeah, yeah...\" Noah gave him a skeptical look. \"One minute before the first class starts. That’s your definition of early?\"","Damien laughed. \"But today I’m more than ten minutes early.\"","\"That’s actually unusual.\"","\"I woke up earlier than usual today.\" Damien stretched his arms behind his head before suddenly remembering something.","\"Oh, right. Master told me something yesterday.\"","\"Hmm?\"","Noah looked at him. \"What did Instructor Morgana tell you?\"","\"She didn’t tell me much.\"","Damien’s grin widened. \"She just said we’d get to hear something interesting tomorrow.\"","He shrugged.\"So let’s see what she has to say.\"","Noah’s curiosity immediately increased. \"Of course. Now I’m curious too.\"","\"Me too.\"","The two continued walking together. By the time they reached the classroom, several students were already inside.","The room was filled with the usual morning atmosphere.","Some students were chatting in small groups, while others were reviewing their notes. A few were leaning against their desks, talking about training from the previous day, while several students were still half-asleep and resting their heads on their arms.","The scrape of chairs against the floor mixed with the low hum of conversations.","Noah entered and immediately headed toward his usual seat. He chose the chair beside Lyria.","Damien sat beside him.","Lyria glanced at Noah with her beautiful pink eyes. For a brief moment, their eyes met. Then she quietly looked forward again.","Noah smiled faintly at her cute reaction.","The classroom gradually filled. One student after another entered until almost every seat was occupied.","The chatter continued for another minute.","The classroom door opened. Instructor Morgana walked inside.","The moment the students saw her, the noise began to die down.","Morgana walked to the front of the classroom with her usual calm expression and placed a few documents on the desk.","She looked across the room. \"Good morning, everyone.\"","\"\"\"Good morning, Instructor Morgana!!!\"\"\"","The students responded almost simultaneously.","Morgana nodded. \"Before we begin today’s lesson, I would like to make an announcement.\"","The remaining whispers immediately disappeared.","Several students straightened in their seats. An announcement from an instructor usually meant something important.","Morgana folded her hands in front of herself. \"It’s regarding your second unit test next month.\"","A few students immediately relaxed. \"Next month?\"","\"We still have plenty of time.\"","\"Wait, another test already?\"","Quiet murmurs spread through the classroom.","Morgana waited for a few seconds before continuing.","\"Yes. You still have plenty of time. The test will be held after the middle of next month.\"","Several students visibly relaxed.","\"However, I thought it would be better to inform you in advance so that you can prepare accordingly.\"","She paused.","\"And unlike the first semester, this examination will not involve a practical battle or a virtual reality match.\"","The classroom became noticeably quieter.","Morgana continued. \"This time, there will be a written examination only.\"","A collective groan immediately swept through the room. \"What?!\"","\"A written exam?\"","\"That’s worse!\"","\"I’d rather fight monsters!\"","A few students laughed, while others dramatically dropped their heads onto their desks.","Noah couldn’t help but smile.","Morgana remained completely unfazed.","\"Considering everything that has happened over the last few months, the academy has decided that it would be more appropriate to exercise greater caution.\"","She looked over the students.","\"So, for this particular examination, you will only need to study.\"","One student raised his fist.","\"That’s not comforting, Instructor!\"","A few students laughed again.","Morgana sighed lightly.","\"I was not finished.\"","The laughter immediately died down. \"But the more interesting announcement comes after that.\"","The students became attentive again.","Morgana picked up one of the documents from her desk.","\"After considerable discussion among the academy staff, we have decided to resume our usual field trips.\"","A wave of excitement immediately spread through the classroom.","\"Field trip?\"","\"Really?\"","\"Where are we going?\"","\"Please don’t tell me it’s dungeon!\"","\"Anywhere but a dungeon!\"","Morgana waited for the noise to settle before continuing.","\"This time, however, we have chosen a rather special destination.\"","The room gradually quieted.","\"Rather than visiting another location within the Aurellian Empire...\"","She paused deliberately.","\"...your next field trip will take you to another country.\"","The classroom exploded.","\"Another country?!\"","\"Seriously?!\"","\"Which one?\"","\"Is that even allowed?\"","Noah’s eyebrows rose. Even he hadn’t expected that.","Morgana finally revealed the destination.","\"The country we have selected is the Elven Kingdom of Elythraen.\"","A few students gasped. Others immediately began whispering excitedly among themselves.","\"The Elven Kingdom...\"","\"I’ve always wanted to see elven nation!\"","\"Do you think we’ll meet the royal family?\"","Morgana raised one hand, bringing the room back under control.","\"You will be visiting the capital city.\"","She spoke clearly.","\"Lunathiel.\"","The name alone caused another wave of excited murmurs. The capital of Elythraen. The heart of the elven kingdom. A place most students had only ever read about in history books.","Morgana continued.","\"And before anyone asks, yes, the Queen will be present in the capital during your visit.\"","The room became unusually quiet.","\"The Queen herself?\"","\"Well her home is there idiots.\"","\"So we can see world tree?!\"","Morgana gave them a small smile.","\"Naturally, the royal family will have strong security measures in place. You will not need to worry about your safety.\"","That was supposed to reassure them. Instead, the students became even more excited.","Noah, however, wasn’t excited at all. His expression had gone completely blank.","’Fuck this.’","His instincts were screaming at him.","’ Another incident is going to happen .’","He leaned back slightly in his chair and stared ahead.He had spent the past few weeks wondering when something troublesome would finally happen.","Now he had his answer.","’I actually thought the academy would avoid sending us anywhere outside the city after everything that happened. And no matter how much academy tries to keep students safe, it will be useless since that’s what story of game needed.’","And also now they weren’t merely leaving the city. They were leaving the empire.","And they were going straight to the capital of another kingdom.","Noah’s expression darkened.","One particular person immediately came to mind.","’Ken.’","His eyes narrowed.","’There’s no way this is a coincidence.’","Ken Takeane had already given Marina an Everbloom Draught. He had asked her to arrange a meeting with the Elven Queen.","And now, somehow, Noah’s class was being sent directly to Lunathiel.","’Ken knows something that going to happen.’","Noah’s fingers slowly tightened.","’Something is going to happen in Lunathiel.’","He stared at the front of the classroom while the excited voices of his classmates continued around him."]},{"number":337,"title":"Chapter 337: Maybe you don’t actually hate these rumors","paragraphs":["===STATUS===","Name: Lyria Sunweave","Race: Human","Age: 19 Years","Strength: 602","Speed: 597","Stamina: 599","Endurance: 590","Charm: 811","Mana: 6083","Core Rank: Condensed (Mid)","Potential: Sovereign Core (High)","Profession: [Spearmanship Lv.3], [Priestess Lv.3]","Technique: [Radiant Spear Art], [Mana Fist Art]","Affinity: Light","Spells: [Light Bullet],[Sphere of light], [Light Lance], [Heal], [Light Cannon], [Augmentation Buffer], [Cleansing Light], [Healing Touch], [Aegis of Light], [Flash Burst],[Light Prison]","Innate Ability: [Purification]","Passive Abilities: [Light of Hope], [Divine Resistance]","======","Classes had ended for the day.","Lyria walked through the academy corridors alongside Arisha and Emma, her footsteps quiet against the polished floor.","While the three girls made their way toward the dormitory area, Lyria’s attention was focused elsewhere. A translucent status window floated before her.","She quietly examined her current abilities and statistics, comparing them to what they had been before.","Her strength had increased. Her mana had grown considerably. Her techniques had improved.","’ I’m getting stronger...but still it’s slow compare to Noah or Damien... I need to work more hard!’","Lyria stared at her status but not for long.","\"I am really excited to visit the Elven Kingdom!\"","Emma’s cheerful voice pulled her out of her thoughts.","Lyria blinked and closed the status window.","Emma’s face was glowing with excitement. \"I’ve never been there before.\"","\"Neither have I,\" Arisha replied casually.","She walked between Emma and Lyria, her long violet hair swaying smoothly with every step.","\"This will be my first time as well.\"","Emma’s excitement grew even more. \"Hey, Lyria. What about you? Have you ever been to the Elven Kingdom?\"","Lyria nodded. \"Yes. I’ve been there a few times.\"","Her expression became slightly nostalgic. \"But the last time I visited was when I was twelve.\"","\"Oh!\"","Emma’s eyes widened. \"Were you there on vacation?\"","\"No.\" Lyria shook her head. \"My family is devoted to the Sun God, as you know. My father occasionally travels to the Elven Kingdom for religious visits.\"","\"Is that because of the World Tree?\"","\"Yes.\"","Lyria nodded.","\"The World Tree is said to contain the essence of prosperity and life. According to the legends, it protects the elves from many dangers.\"","Her voice became slightly softer as she explained. \"It is also said to have been a gift from the Sun God to the elves. And according to their beliefs, a deity of life resides within the tree—a daughter of the Sun God. So many consider the world tree as daughter of Sun God.\"","\"Wow~\"","Emma’s eyes sparkled. \"So the World Tree really has a deity living inside it?\"","\"That’s what the legends say.\" Lyria smiled faintly. \"Because of that, my family also visits the tree to pray whenever we travel there.\"","She paused. \"Unfortunately, I don’t remember much from my first visit. I was very young and didn’t even understand how to properly speak with others.\"","Emma chuckled. \"And you visited again when you were twelve?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"So it’s been quite a while since you’ve been there.\"","\"Indeed.\"","Lyria nodded.","\"Why didn’t you visit again?\" Arisha asked.","\"It was mostly because it wasn’t compulsory.\" Lyria shrugged slightly. \"My family considers the pilgrimage important, but I wasn’t required to accompany my father every time. After that, I became more focused on training and studying.\"","Arisha nodded in understanding. \"Then I’m more than ready to go.\"","She glanced ahead. \"And as for danger... well, we joined the academy to become stronger. We can’t spend our entire lives playing it safe.\"","\"I think the same!\" Emma enthusiastically bumped her fist into her palm.","\"Besides, we’re going to another country! How could I not be excited?\"","Lyria smiled at their enthusiasm. But their peaceful conversation was soon interrupted.","\"That’s Lyria, isn’t it?\"","A voice came from behind them. \"I heard she’s in a relationship with Noah.\"","\"What? Really?\"","\"I thought that was just a rumor.\"","The voices were quiet, but the academy corridor was relatively calm, allowing the words to reach Lyria’s ears clearly.","Her footsteps slowed. A faint blush immediately appeared across her cheeks.","Arisha noticed. \"Are you alright, Lyria?\" She glanced at her friend. \"Are those rumors bothering you?\"","\"No.\" Lyria quickly shook her head. \"They aren’t. I’m not worried about them at all.\"","Emma smiled. \"That’s good. Hopefully, the rumors haven’t reached your father yet.\"","Lyria smiled gently. \"It’s alright. In the end, they’re only rumors.\"","She wasn’t particularly worried. \"My father trusts me. Even if he heard them and had doubts, he would simply ask me about it, and I could tell him the truth.\"","Arisha suddenly gave her a teasing look. \"Hmm...\"","Lyria immediately became suspicious. \"What?\"","\"Maybe you don’t actually hate these rumors.\" Arisha’s lips curled into a mischievous smile. \"Perhaps you secretly like being called Noah’s lover.\"","\"What?!\" Lyria’s face instantly turned red.","\"Of course that’s not the case, Arisha!\"","She covered part of her burning face. \"You know that! Stop making fun of me!\"","Emma laughed. \"Yeah, there’s no way Lyria would actually like Noah.\"","Arisha raised one eyebrow. \"And why is that?\"","She looked at Lyria with an amused expression.","\"He’s the second-ranked student, talented, strong for his age, and considerably more handsome than he used to be. Not forgetting how many times he got in danger and survived them.\"","Lyria’s face became even redder.","Arisha continued mercilessly. \"He has also changed quite a lot since returning to the academy. And he has shown some interest in her several times.\"","\"W-Well...\" Lyria hesitated. \"I mean... you’re not wrong.\"","Emma’s eyebrows rose. \"Wait, you’re actually agreeing with her?\"","\"N-No! That’s not what I meant!\" Lyria hurriedly defended herself.","Arisha chuckled. \"There’s also the matter of Ophelia.\"","Lyria and Emma both looked at her. \"It seems the bitterness between her and Noah has decreased considerably. I’ve seen her talking to him and greeting him several times.\"","Arisha shrugged. \"Perhaps it’s because of her mother.\"","\"Now that you mention it...\" Emma placed a finger against her chin.","\"They don’t seem to be on bad terms anymore.\"","She glanced at Lyria. \"So maybe Noah isn’t such a bad choice for you.\"","\"H-Hey!\" Lyria’s face turned completely crimson. \"You two are going too far!\"","She finally raised her voice, clearly losing her patience with their constant teasing. \"Why are the two of you deciding things for me?!\"","Arisha and Emma exchanged amused glances. \"Hehe.\"","\"Lyria is cute when she’s flustered.\"","\"Very cute.\"","Neither girl showed any intention of stopping.","Lyria’s cheeks puffed slightly. Then she pointed a trembling finger directly at Arisha.","\"Y-You!\"","Arisha blinked innocently. \"He has shown more interest in you than he has in me!\"","Lyria’s accusation left Emma momentarily speechless.","Arisha, however, remained completely unfazed. She casually ran a hand through her long violet hair.","\"I don’t mind.\"","\"What?\"","\"If he wants to flirt with me, then he can.\" Arisha gave a small shrug. \"Perhaps he might even manage to win my heart.\"","Lyria’s pink eyes widened.","She had expected her words to embarrass Arisha or at least make her deny it. Instead, Arisha had calmly accepted the possibility.","Even Emma looked slightly surprised. Perhaps she was only teasing Lyria and deliberately turning the tables on her.","But judging by Arisha’s calm expression, it was impossible to tell.","Lyria stared at her for several seconds.","\"You... you are a terrible woman!\" She turned around and marched ahead.","\"Hey! Wait for us!\" Emma hurried after her.","\"Hey, Lyria! I’m sorry!\" Arisha followed as well, laughing softly.","The three girls continued down the corridor together, their voices gradually fading into the bustling academy halls."]},{"number":338,"title":"Chapter 338: What Should I do?","paragraphs":["\"What should I do?\"","Noah lay on his bed, staring at the ceiling as he thought about the danger that might be waiting ahead.","He had no solid evidence against Ken. The young man merely seemed suspicious because of the things he had done, particularly his strange interest in meeting the Elven Queen.","But could Noah actually confront him? Could he simply ask Ken whether he was a transmigrator?","There were too many possible outcomes.","Even if Noah confronted him and discovered that Ken really was a transmigrator with knowledge of the future, what were the chances that he would not be hostile?","What if Ken refused to cooperate with him? What if he saw Noah as a threat?","Worse, what if Ken deliberately fed him false information about the future and tried to manipulate him?","Noah himself was not a bad person, nor was he some ruthless villain.","However, he had read enough webnovels to know that transmigrated protagonists were not always kind-hearted heroes.","Many of them were villains or antiheroes—people willing to do morally questionable things, betray others, or even sacrifice innocent people if it meant surviving or achieving their goals.","To be honest, as a reader, Noah actually preferred those kinds of protagonists over the typical righteous heroes.","Villains and antiheroes were simply more interesting.","But now that he was actually living inside a game world, he desperately hoped that if Ken really was a transmigrator, he wasn’t some cold-blooded bastard who viewed everyone around him as disposable pawns.","’What a mess... Guess villains are only cool in novels, not in real life. Shit.’","There was also another possibility. Ken might not be a transmigrator at all.","Noah could simply be misunderstanding everything.","And if that was the case, confronting Ken would make things even more awkward. Noah could always dismiss his suspicions afterward, but what if Ken also had his own reasons for hiding certain things?","There was another problem.","If Ken really was a transmigrator, there was a good chance he had already realized that the current Noah was not the same person as the Noah from the original story.","After all, Noah’s personality had changed far too much.","If Ken knew the original story, he would probably have noticed it.","Noah cursed his luck.","He had been thrown into this world without any knowledge of what happened after the game’s original storyline.","He had no idea what the future held. He had no guide. Once again he felt useless.","With a tired sigh, Noah shook his head. For now, there was no reason to burden himself with endless possibilities.","The only thing he could do was observe. He shouldn’t act recklessly and expose his suspicions without enough evidence.","’I’ll just keep watching Ken for now.’","With that decision made, Noah closed his eyes.","He decided to sleep.","---","Next day.","\"Hello, Ken. We haven’t really talked much since the academy started.\"","Noah sat beside Ken during class while their instructor continued his lecture.","Today’s lesson was about monsters and beast-related knowledge.","Instructor Liam, an elderly man with a rather serious expression, stood at the front of the classroom. A large projection covered the wall behind him, displaying images of various Rank D and Rank C monsters while he explained their characteristics, habitats, and dangerous traits.","\"Yeah. Hello.\"","Ken replied casually, his dark-gray eyes remaining fixed on the projection. He was surprisingly attentive. He didn’t even glance at Noah.","’This guy... is really focused on studying.’","Noah also turned his attention toward the lesson. After a few seconds, however, he leaned slightly toward Ken.","\"By the way, are you excited about the field trip to the Elven Kingdom?\"","That finally made Ken turn toward him.","’Yeah! You must know I’m a transmigrator! Come on, Ken! Reveal yourself! Say that you need to tell me something important!’","\"Yes, actually. I’m quite excited.\"","Ken gave him a small smile. \"I’ve never been there before, so I think it will be an amazing experience.\"","With that, he turned his attention back toward the projection.","Noah’s lips twitched.","’Fair enough.’","He had to admit, Ken’s response was perfectly normal. There was nothing suspicious about it.","Noah leaned back in his chair and continued watching the lesson.","His thoughts briefly wandered toward his own abilities.","His sword technique, especially the one he used with his katana, allowed him to unleash an almost instantaneous slash.","The technique involved drawing the blade from its sheath and returning it before most people could even see the movement.","It was incredibly cool.","Noah couldn’t help but feel a little proud whenever he thought about it. Then, after a moment, another thought crossed his mind.","\"Hey...\"","Noah glanced at Ken.","\"I’ve mostly seen you together with Marina. Are you two dating or something?\"","Ken stiffened. It was subtle, but Noah noticed it immediately. The tips of Ken’s ears turned slightly red, and he quickly looked at Noah.","\"What are you saying?!\"","His usually calm expression was replaced by clear embarrassment. \"We’re just good friends! There’s nothing between us!\"","His voice rose slightly as he defended himself.","Noah raised an eyebrow. ’Oh? Interesting.’","Before he could ask anything else.","\"YOU TWO! STAND UP!\"","Both Noah and Ken flinched. They immediately stood from their seats. Instructor Liam glared at them from the front of the classroom, his expression darkening.","\"You two dare to chat during my class?!\"","He slammed his hand against the desk.","\"Now tell me! What was the sentence I spoke immediately before I caught you two talking?\"","Silence.","Noah and Ken looked at each other. Neither of them had the slightest idea.","\"...\"","\"...\"","Instructor Liam’s face twitched. \"You weren’t listening?!\"","He immediately launched into another furious lecture.","Meanwhile, Leonard, Damien, and Arisha watched the scene from their seats. Leonard was trying not to laugh.","Damien openly grinned. Even Arisha had a faint smile on her face as she watched Noah and Ken suffer under Instructor Liam’s wrath.","Noah could only sigh inwardly.","’Well... at least I learned one thing. Ken definitely doesn’t like being teased about Marina.’","But whether that meant anything more remained unknown."]},{"number":339,"title":"Chapter 339: To Elythraen","paragraphs":["The days passed faster than Noah had expected. He spent most of his time training, thinking about the future, teasing his friends, and missing Akari.","Whenever he had some free time, he would call her. During one of their conversations, Akari told him something interesting.","The Emperor, Viserys Augustus, had summoned her to meet him. And she had gone.","At the time, Akari had been busy and hadn’t explained their conversation in detail. However, a few days before Noah’s unit test, she finally told him everything that had happened during their meeting.","Noah found one part of it rather amusing.","The Emperor hadn’t summoned him at all.","Apparently, Viserys had been more interested in hearing things directly from Akari rather than questioning Noah about his own experience.","Honestly, Noah wasn’t complaining. If anything, he was relieved.","He really didn’t want to meet the Emperor.","And also he failed at trying to find more evidence or hints about Ken being transmgrator.","\"This much should be enough.\"","Noah stood beside his bed, looking over everything he had packed. A few changes of clothes.","Several potions, few rolls of gauze and some bandages. Despite having healing potions, he took this things after all when he’s too much injured, even healing potions doesn’t work well.","He checked everything one more time before nodding.","The unit test had ended a day ago, and now it was finally time for their trip to the Elven Kingdom. Most students agreed to have this.","They would be staying there for four days.","The trip wasn’t meant to be purely recreational. The academy wanted the students to learn about another nation’s culture, beliefs, lifestyle, history, and environment.","’We might even get the chance to meet some major figures from the kingdom.’","Noah paused. ’Especially the Queen.’","After spending months in this world, Noah felt that he had experienced at least a little character development.","Or, at least, that’s what he liked to believe.","For once, he wasn’t particularly excited about meeting a beautiful elven queen.","’Enough chasing after beautiful women. From now on, I need to be a proper gentleman.’","Noah nodded firmly to himself. He felt as though he had just made an incredibly important life decision.","Then his eyes fell on the bed. Nancy was sleeping peacefully.","\"Oh, my Nancy!\"","Noah’s expression immediately softened. \"How am I supposed to live without you for four whole days? Come here, my little cutie.\"","He scooped up the sleeping cat and immediately began showering her with kisses.","Nancy didn’t even bother opening her eyes. She simply remained limp in his arms, completely unbothered by her owner’s affection.","Noah believed that Nancy would be perfectly capable of taking care of herself. Even before he had taken her in, she had survived on her own around the academy.","Still, he couldn’t help worrying about her.","\"All the first-year classes are going on field trips to different regions of the world...\"","Noah sighed. \"Well, our entire class A-1 is going to the Elven Kingdom.\"","He glanced down at Nancy. \"And somehow, we’re the ones who have to suffer through this.\"","He thought for a moment. \"Well, I could just take you with me. No big deal—\"","He stopped. \"...No. If something happens, you’ll be in danger.\"","Nancy remained completely relaxed in his arms.","Noah stared at her for a moment before sighing. \"Fine. I’ll leave you with someone I trust.\"","Nancy’s only response was a lazy flick of her tail.","---","After a while the first-year students gathered inside the academy’s gateway hall.","Class A-1 stood in orderly rows while they waited for the teleportation gate to activate.","Most of them were wearing their academy uniforms.","Among them stood Arisha.","Even in the standard academy uniform, she stood out from the crowd. Her long violet hair, striking yellow eyes, and beautiful appearance naturally drew attention.","Standing in front of her was Lyria, whose golden hair and gentle presence were equally noticeable.","Damien and several other students stood farther ahead in the formation.","Lyria glanced around. \"Noah still hasn’t arrived.\"","Arisha, standing behind her, raised an eyebrow. \"Oh? Are you already missing him?\"","\"Shut up!\" Lyria immediately became embarrassed.","\"Hehe.\"","Arisha couldn’t help but laugh. Just then, footsteps approached from behind.","\"Friend, let me stand behind her.\"","Arisha turned around.","Sure enough, Noah had arrived.","He was currently asking the student behind her to move slightly so that he could take the empty spot in the row.","Arisha stared at him. \"Do you really need to stand near us?\"","Noah successfully squeezed into the space and immediately smirked. \"Of course I do. I can’t leave my two ladies alone, can I?\"","A small smile appeared on Arisha’s lips.","That man always tried to say something ridiculous or throw out some cheesy or cringe line whenever he got the chance.","Arisha knew he was only teasing her and trying to have fun. So she always played along.","And, somehow she enjoyed his company more than she would ever admit.","\"A desperate boy, as far as I can see,\" Arisha said casually. \"Right, Lyria?\"","\"What? What’s he desperate for?\"","Lyria looked genuinely confused.","Noah frowned as well. \"Yeah, what am I desperate for?\"","Arisha looked at both of them. \"Obviously, you’re desperate for attention from me and Lyria.\"","\"He-hey! That’s not the case!\" Noah immediately defended himself.","Emma, who was standing in front of Lyria, sighed. \"Damn, you guys have already started again.\"","\"Well I don’t think Noah is like that.\" Lyria tried to defend Noah.","Ignoring Emma’s comment, Arisha looked at Lyria with a teasing smile. \"Oh, my dear Lyria. You’re so innocent.\"","She leaned slightly toward her. \"Noah just wants to get under us, seduce us and you haven’t even noticed.\"","\"Arisha!\" Lyria’s face turned red. \"You always say such embarrassing things!\"","Noah placed a hand against his chest, looking offended. \"Hey! I’m a good man now. I’m not the old Noah anymore. This is my second change. Just observe me, from now on I won’t flirt.\"","He refused to accept the accusation.","Arisha narrowed her eyes. ’You did that just a minute ago.’ She said, \"You already changed once before entering the academy. And I don’t think you need to change again. So don’t.\"","Her expression became slightly more serious. \"I warn you.\"","Noah blinked. Then he placed a hand dramatically over his heart.","\"Oh my~\"","He gave her a playful smile. \"Are you trying to win my heart? Are you hitting on me?\"","Arisha calmly met his gaze. \"Maybe.\"","Noah’s smile froze for a moment.","Arisha continued. \"I just hope you don’t become some bland, boring man. I like you better this way.\"","There was no teasing in her voice this time.","She meant it.","No matter how strange, shameless, or flirtatious Noah could be, she genuinely liked the way he acted around them.","He was free. He was weird. And, most importantly, he was himself.","\"Wh-what? If you’re going to say something like that—\"","Before Noah could finish, a clear voice echoed throughout the gateway hall.","\"Everyone, listen.\"","Instructor Morgana’s voice instantly silenced the students.","She stood beside the enormous circular teleportation gate, which was already glowing with brilliant blue light.","Two other instructors stood beside her. They would be accompanying Class A-1 throughout the trip.","\"All students of our class are present.\"","Morgana looked over the group.","\"Now, enter the teleportation gate one by one. And make sure you have your academy IDs with you.\"","\"YES!\"","The students answered enthusiastically.","One by one, they began moving toward the glowing gate.","Arisha looked forward as she waited for her turn.","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","’We can explore the kingdom together...’","A memory suddenly surfaced in her mind. She remembered the time before summer vacation when the three of them had spent time together.","Just Noah, Lyria, and herself.","The memory brought a small, genuine smile to her face.","’Maybe this trip will be fun too.’"]},{"number":340,"title":"Chapter 340: Lunathiel","paragraphs":["Elythraen was the only major nation on the elven continent of Sylvael, and it had existed for thousands of years.","Unlike the human kingdoms, which had spent centuries fighting one another before eventually uniting under the Aurellian Empire, the elves had never experienced a major war among their own races.","High Elves, Dark Elves, Lunar Elves, Wood Elves, and several other elven races had lived together under the same realm for generations.","Despite their differences in appearance, culture, and magical talents, they all shared something in common.","Their deep connection to nature.","The elves worshipped the Sun God and revered the World Tree, believing that nature itself was a sacred gift that had to be protected.","Noah didn’t know much about elven history. Most of what he knew came from the limited information from the brain of past Noah.","However, there was one elven race that had always caught his attention.","The Lunar Elves. Also known as Moon Elves. The reason was simple. Their name seemed strangely connected to the Moon Goddess.","It wasn’t as though Noah had never tried to learn more about them.","After returning from that mysterious realm, he had spent some time researching the Moon Goddess and the legends surrounding her.","During his research, he had naturally come across the Lunar Elves.","Unfortunately, there wasn’t much information about them.","They worshipped the World Tree and the Sun God just like the other elven races and had done so for generations.","Their name, Lunar Elves, apparently came from their unique appearance.","They possessed pale, frost-blue skin and beautiful silver hair, giving them an almost otherworldly appearance that reminded people of moonlight.","But beyond that there was nothing particularly significant recorded about them.","Noah had found that strange and believes there’s more to it.","If their name was connected to the Moon Goddess, shouldn’t there have been something more?","Before he could think about it any further, a voice came from ahead.","\"Welcome to Lunathiel, the capital city of Elythraen.\"","The voice belonged to an elf standing on the other side of the teleportation gateway.","He appeared to be in his early forties, at least by human standards, though Noah knew appearances could be misleading when it came to elves.","He had long emerald-green hair tied neatly behind his head and sharp green eyes. His features were refined and disciplined.","He wore a dark-green robe reinforced with light armor around the shoulders and chest.","\"I’m pleased to welcome the students and instructors of Novaris Academy.\"","He placed a hand over his chest and gave them a respectful bow.","\"My name is Eldrian Vaelwood. I am a senior mage serving in the defensive forces of Lunathiel. My core rank is Aeternum, mid stage.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed slightly. ’Senior mage? And at Aeternum mid core. That’s great.’","Eldrian straightened and continued.","\"My primary responsibility is the defense of this city and its surrounding territories. I will be accompanying you throughout your stay in Lunathiel.\"","He gestured toward the two elves standing beside him.","\"These are my assistants and fellow members of the city’s defensive forces.\"","The female elf stepped forward first.","She had long silver-green hair, bright emerald eyes, and a graceful appearance. Unlike Eldrian, she wore a lighter combat outfit consisting of a fitted green uniform and light leather armor.","\"My name is Elowen Silaris.\"","She gave the students a gentle smile.","\"I specialize in magical archery and reconnaissance. It is a pleasure to meet all of you.\"","The male elf beside her stepped forward next.","He had short dark-green hair and calm blue eyes. His attire was similar to Eldrian’s, though his armor was lighter.","\"I am Caelan Thornwood. I specialize in defensive magic and barrier techniques.\"","He gave a short bow. \"I hope your stay in Lunathiel will be both enjoyable and educational.\"","\"Thank you for welcoming us.\"","Instructor Morgana stepped forward.","She was dressed differently from her usual academy attire today.","She wore a beautiful dark-violet blouse paired with a fitted pencil skirt, along with black, semi-transparent stockings and elegant high heels.","Her appearance was striking enough that several male students couldn’t help stealing glances at her.","She looked beautiful and strict.","And somehow, she had the kind of presence that made even grown men feel as though getting scolded by her might not be such a terrible experience.","Noah glanced at her. Then immediately looked away.","’What the hell am I even thinking?! I have already decided to be a good man!’","He mentally slapped himself.","Morgana continued speaking.","\"Eldrian and his team will be accompanying us throughout our entire stay in Lunathiel.\"","She looked toward the students.","\"They will teach you about the history, culture, traditions, and beliefs of Elythraen. You will also have opportunities to learn directly from them about magic, archery, magical reconnaissance, and defensive techniques.\"","The students immediately became more interested.","Several of them exchanged excited looks.","Learning directly from an Aeternum-level mage and experienced members of the city’s defense forces was an opportunity they wouldn’t normally get.","\"Now,\" Eldrian said with a smile, \"if you would follow us, I believe your first impression of Lunathiel should be the city itself.\"","The group began moving. They passed through the gateway hall and finally stepped outside.","The moment Noah emerged, he stopped. His eyes widened. \"...Whoa.\"","Lunathiel stretched out before them.","It was enormous. The city was nothing like the human cities Noah had visited before.","Massive trees grew throughout the streets, their branches forming natural canopies over roads and walkways.","Many of the buildings had been constructed around enormous trees rather than cutting them down.","Some houses seemed to grow directly from the trunks, while others had been built using specially treated wood and living vines.","Greenery covered almost everything. Vines climbed across walls. Flowers grew along rooftops.","Small trees stood between buildings. Even the roads had been designed around the existing landscape rather than replacing it.","Yet Lunathiel wasn’t some primitive city frozen in the past.","Noah quickly noticed magical machines operating throughout the streets.","Transportation devices moved along designated paths. Magical lamps for illuminung the roads at night.","And large projection screens were attached to several buildings, displaying information, announcements, advertisements, and various magical images.","The screens themselves were surrounded by vines and greenery, blending modern technology with nature so seamlessly that they almost looked like they belonged there.","The elves had clearly developed their own version of modern civilization. They simply refused to sacrifice nature for it.","’So this is how the elves developed...’","Noah looked around in fascination. It was both advanced and natural. Modern, yet deeply connected to the environment.","But there was one thing that immediately dwarfed everything else.","At the heart of Lunathiel stood an enormous tree.","Noah slowly raised his head. And kept raising it.","The trunk was so massive that it looked more like a mountain than a tree.","Its enormous branches spread across the sky, extending over a some portion of the city.","Countless smaller branches reached outward like enormous arms, covered in brilliant green leaves.","The canopy stretched so far that it almost seemed to create a second sky above Lunathiel.","And the tree it seemed to touch the heavens.","Noah stood there silently. His eyes widened with genuine admiration.","’Now this is what you call fantasy world...’","There was no mistaking it. He had seen images on internet. But nothing could have prepared him for seeing it with his own eyes.","The World Tree, the sacred tree of the elves. And the symbol of Elythraen.","Noah stared at it as this tree left him more speechless than anything else.","’So this is the World Tree...’"]},{"number":341,"title":"Chapter 341: Some History Lessons [1]","paragraphs":["\"Alright. Firstly, we’re going to visit a region outside the city where a major battle took place.\"","Eldrian’s voice echoed through the transport vehicle.","\"Approximately one hundred and seven years ago, this area became one of the main battlefields during the war between Elythraen and the vampire kingdom.\"","The students immediately became more attentive. Noah sat beside the window, looking outside as the vehicle moved through Lunathiel. The vehicle was huge bus like structure.","Outside the city itself was a sight worth remembering.","Massive trees towered over the streets, their branches stretching between buildings and forming enormous natural canopies.","Elven architecture blended seamlessly with nature.","Some buildings had been constructed around trees, while others seemed to grow directly from them. Vines covered walls and balconies, flowers grew along rooftops, and magical lamps hung from branches like glowing fruits.","Somehow, none of it felt out of place. Everything had been designed to coexist with nature rather than dominate it.","Noah rested his chin against his hand as he watched the scenery pass.","’This place really is beautiful.’","The farther they traveled from the center of the city, however, the fewer buildings they saw. The massive trees gradually became more scattered.","After approximately thirty minutes, the vehicles finally slowed down.","\"We’re here.\"","Eldrian stood.","The students looked outside with curiosity. The scenery had changed completely. There was a vast open area stretching across the land.","Noah immediately found it strange. ’An open field... in the middle of the Elven Kingdom?’","The elves were famous for their deep connection with nature. Trees covered most of Elythraen, and even the cities were built around them.","Yet this enormous region was almost completely devoid of trees.","Instead, ruins covered the landscape.","Broken walls, collapsed towers and half-buried stone structures. Fragments of ancient buildings were scattered across the ground.","Moss covered the remains, while thick vines crawled over broken walls and twisted around fallen pillars.","Some structures were so badly damaged that it was difficult to tell what they had originally been.","The students stepped out of the vehicles. Everyone looked around with curiosity.","\"This place...\"","Lyria murmured.","\"It feels like an ancient ruin.\"","\"It is,\" Eldrian replied.","He raised his voice so everyone could hear.","\"This region used to be part of Lunathiel itself.\"","Several students looked surprised.","\"The city was considerably larger more than a century ago as there were not many great cities, at current time there are many huge cities rivaling capital... so people moved out. At that time, one of the major military bases of the Elythraen army was located here.\"","Eldrian pointed toward the largest cluster of ruins. \"You can still see some of its remains.\"","Noah looked toward the ruins. Noah muttered. \"So this used to be a military base?\"","Eldrian continued. \"During that period, the vampire kingdom of Vespermark was still active.\"","The students became noticeably quieter. Even those who knew little about history had heard of Vespermark.","The supposedly extinct vampire kingdom.","\"The vampires had been hostile toward Elythraen for generations,\" Eldrian continued. \"They frequently crossed our borders in secret. Some of their forces abducted elves and transported them back to Vespermark.\"","His expression became noticeably colder. \"Some were used as slaves.\"","A few students frowned.","\"Others...\" Eldrian paused. \"...were used as food. Well most of them were like blood bags.\"","The atmosphere immediately became heavier.","Noah’s expression hardened slightly. He had already read about the vampires before.","But hearing the history directly from an elf who had inherited those memories through generations made it feel different.","\"At the time, our kingdom attempted to avoid a full-scale war,\" Eldrian continued. \"The elves had no desire to invade Vespermark, nor did we wish to shed blood unnecessarily.\"","\"But eventually, the situation became impossible to ignore.\"","Eldrian looked toward the distant ruins.","\"The incident that triggered the war occurred at the border.\"","The students listened carefully.","\"Approximately one hundred and seven years ago, the youngest prince of Vespermark, Varex Noctharis, personally led a small group of vampires across the border.\"","Several students exchanged glances.","\"Varex was reckless and arrogant. He had planned to abduct the young princess of Elythraen, Princess Aelyssa Sylvaine, who was traveling near the border under the protection of several elven guards.\"","Noah raised his brow. ’That’s... the current queen..’","Eldrian’s expression darkened. \"His intention was to take her back to Vespermark and present her to his father, King Malverion Noctharis, as a gift. If might be aware that elven blood, especially that of high elves blood of royal family was considered best for vampires. And that Varex wanted his father to favor him to be next king.\"","\"What happened then?\" one of the students asked.","\"A powerful elven mage discovered them.\"","Eldrian’s eyes narrowed.","\"His name was Theron Vaelcrest, one of the strongest battle mages of Elythraen at the time. Theron confronted Varex before the vampires could escape.\"","A brief silence followed. \"Varex was killed at the border.\"","The students remained silent.","\"That should have been the end of the incident,\" Eldrian continued. \"Unfortunately, King Malverion did not see it that way.\"","His voice became colder.","\"He declared that Elythraen had murdered a member of the royal family and ordered his armies to mobilize.\"","Noah frowned. ’So the kidnapping attempt became the spark that started the war.’","\"Vampire forces invaded Elythraen soon afterward.\"","Eldrian gestured toward the ruins surrounding them.","\"This area became one of the primary battlefields.\"","The students looked around.","\"At the time, the city defenses were positioned here because this was one of the main entrances into Lunathiel.\"","Eldrian pointed toward several collapsed structures.","\"Those ruins were once military barracks, defensive towers, storage facilities, and mage formations.\"","Noah looked carefully at the ground.","Even after more than a century, faint traces of magical formations could still be seen beneath the moss.","\"The battle lasted for several days.\"","Eldrian’s expression became solemn.","\"The vampires were extremely difficult to fight. Their regenerative abilities made them dangerous opponents, especially during close combat. But we had one advantage.\"","He looked toward the students.","\"We were fighting on our own territory.\"","The elves had extensive knowledge of the surrounding forests, terrain, magical formations, and defensive routes.","\"After several battles, the Elythraen army managed to push the vampires back.\"","Eldrian paused.","\"Eventually, Vespermark’s forces were defeated.\"","Some students quietly exhaled.","\"So the elves won?\" Damien asked.","\"Yes.\"","Eldrian nodded.","\"But victory came at a considerable cost.\"","His expression became more serious.","\"Many elves died.\"","The students fell silent.","\"However, the vampires were not our only enemy.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed. He asked this time curiously. \"What do you mean?\"","Eldrian looked toward the ruins.","\"We discovered that several elves had secretly betrayed Elythraen.\""]},{"number":342,"title":"Chapter 342: Some History Lessons [2]","paragraphs":["A murmur spread through the students after hearing it. After all many people study more about their own country’s history that others. Same goes for human empire, even academy mostly taught their own history more. And some involving other countries.","\"Some had accepted payment from the vampires. Others had been promised positions and wealth if Vespermark conquered our kingdom.\"","He paused. \"And some had helped the vampires enter our territory by revealing military information and hidden routes.\"","Noah frowned. ’So there were traitors inside the kingdom.’","\"Even elves are not always trustworthy,\" Eldrian said quietly.","His words carried no anger but only disappointment.","\"But there is another part of this history that you should understand.\"","The students became attentive again.","\"Long before the war with Vespermark, there was another group connected to the vampires.\"","Eldrian looked toward the distant horizon. \"The Blood Elves.\"","Several students immediately began whispering among themselves.","Noah’s expression changed slightly. ’Blood Elves?’","He had heard the name before.","\"Thousands of years ago, the Blood Elves were originally part of the greater elven civilization.\"","Eldrian explained.","\"They possessed many characteristics similar to ordinary elves, but their culture revolved around the consumption and manipulation of blood.\"","\"Over time, their practices became increasingly violent. They began secretly attacking other elves and draining their blood.\"","His voice hardened. \"Some even experimented on other races elves. The ancient elven kingdom eventually banished them from our lands as always being kind nature. They fled to the territories that become part of Vespermark.\"","Eldrian glanced toward the students.","\"Over the centuries, the Blood Elves became closely associated with the vampire race. Some eventually call themselves vampires rather than elves,\"","\"So they were already living with the vampires before the war?\" Lyria asked.","\"Yes.\"","Eldrian nodded.","\"Those elves were hard to differentiate from normal so many were mixed in our kingdom and helped vampires. That is why the history between elves and vampires is far older and more complicated than the war you have just learned about. After the war our king left the world peacefully in hand of his daughter, princess Aelyssa and now she’s our queen and pride.\"","The students began murmuring among themselves.","Noah remained silent. He couldn’t help thinking about what Akari had told him.","Vampires were supposedly extinct. Yet there were still too many strange connections surrounding them.","Bloodmoon Rot and everbloom Draught which he learned from Ken and Marina.","And now Blood Elves. There’s definitely some connection between origin of blood elves and vampires","’There are way too many coincidences.’ Noah quietly sighed. ’I really hope I’m just being paranoid.’","After spending some time examining the ruins and listening to Eldrian’s explanations, the students eventually returned to their vehicles.","After that the group saw few more places, they also eat few dishes that could be found only in elven kingdom.","After lunch in noon, they were led to forest. As instructor told them to go and hunt as practice.","They were able to see many different kind of monsters such as Mossfang Bear, A -D rank massive bear covered in thick moss and fungal growth. Its hide is extremely tough, and its claws contain a natural poison.","The three elves together with all students taught them about monsters first that were found in forest.","Especiallt Verdant Stalker, a large feline-like predator covered in moss and leaves. It can camouflage itself perfectly among ancient trees and attack by manipulating vines.","They hunt monster spreading around for hours, amusing thing that many elves were hidden in different part of forest, in trees, constantly looking at students and also for protection of city.","As evening came, the group traveling through the outskirts of Lunathiel before finally arriving at a large complex.","Noah sitting beside Arisha thought. ’The first day went without any problem, I thought something might happened.’","He looked around students who were laughing and chatting. ’What a lucky students they are, enjoying their lif-’","Suddenly remembering what he had gone through. ’Maybe not... sigh don’t know how long they will laugh and enjoy like this.’","\"What are you thinking so deeply about?\" Leonardo’s voice broke Noah from his thoughts.","\"Nothing..\" Noah look sideways. He sat in row beside him, Kaelan was there. Silently watching outside.","Students were slowly getting out one by one.","Once outside, a massive wooden structure stood before them.","Unlike the ruins they had just visited, this building was well maintained.","Its architecture blended perfectly with the surrounding trees, with several large branches growing around the structure without damaging it.","There were multiple floors and countless rooms inside. \"This is where all of you will be staying for the next four days,\" Morgana announced.","The students immediately became excited.","Morgana raised one hand.","\"However, there will be rules.\"","The excitement died down slightly.","\"You will be staying two students per room. Your room assignments have already been decided.\"","She began calling out the names one by one.","Students gradually picked up their belongings and headed toward their assigned rooms.","Eventually, Noah looked at Damien. \"Why did I end up with you?\"","Damien raised an eyebrow. \"Don’t look so disappointed.\"","\"I’m not disappointed.\" Noah lied. \"I’m just wondering why we were paired together.\"","\"Because the instructor probably thinks we’re good friends.\" Damien chuckled and said it.","Noah nodded. \"Yeah. That might be the reason.\"","The two walked toward the elevator.","Unlike a normal human elevator, the one inside the building had been constructed almost entirely from enchanted wood.","Beautiful carvings decorated the walls, depicting trees, flowers, animals, and various elven symbols.","As the elevator began moving upward, one entire side of the structure opened toward the outside.","Through the transparent magical barrier, Noah and Damien could see the beautiful city of Lunathiel stretching beneath them.","The enormous trees, the vine-covered buildings and the glowing magical lights.","And, in the distance the towering World Tree.","Damien stared outside with an excited smile.","\"Man, this place is incredible.\"","Noah nodded. \"Yeah.\"","His gaze remained fixed on the city.","’Today’s information was good... I guess I should visit some library in this kingdom and read about history.’","Noah hated reading history. But sometimes a person needed to do something they hate it. And he had a feeling those four days were going to be anything but peaceful."]},{"number":343,"title":"Chapter 343: Th-this... What is the meaning of this, young man?","paragraphs":["\"So, when was the time you came to this city? And from where?\"","Noah leaned casually against the counter of a small perfume shop, his eyes wandering over the colorful bottles displayed behind the counter.","Today was second day of their field trip and instructor had allow them to roam the city. So the group came to the shop while exploring near by places.","\"It was about twenty years ago. We came from the southern region, from the territory of Silunara. It is one of the domains controlled by the Great Houses of the Elven Kingdom, House Selunaris. Silunara has been the homeland of the Moon Elves for centuries, and House Selunaris has ruled over the region for generations.\"","The woman standing behind the counter smiled gently.","She was a beautiful Lunar Elf with sky-blue skin, shoulder-length silver hair, and striking glacier-blue eyes. Her appearance was youthful enough to make her look like she was in her early twenties.","She wore an elegant white robe with a V-shaped neckline, revealing just enough of her figure to give the outfit a graceful yet alluring appearance.","Her eyes remained fixed on Noah, clearly amused by the young man’s interest in her.","\"Twenty years ago?\" Noah tilted his head. \"My, my... You must have been such a cute little girl back then.\"","The woman immediately laughed, placing a hand against her cheek. \"Oh, no, no. I wasn’t a child at all. I was already an adult back then.\"","\"Haha, is that so?\" Noah looked her up and down before smiling. \"It’s just hard to tell from your appearance. You look like a woman in her twenties.\"","\"My, you certainly have a sweet tongue.\" She covered her smile with one hand.","\"But you should know that elves have long lifespans. We age much more slowly than humans. Even a normal elf who never chase the power and increase his core rank can live upto 200 years.\"","\"Of course, I’m aware of that.\"","Noah nodded. \"Even so, you look like someone who should still be attending the academy rather than running a shop.\"","The Lunar Elf’s cheeks immediately turned slightly pink. \"Come now. You’re going to make me blush.\"","Noah smiled. At that moment, he had completely forgotten the vow he had made only yesterday.","’Enough chasing beautiful women. From now on, I need to be a proper gentleman.’","Apparently, that resolution had lasted less than a day.","Several meters away, his friends were watching the entire scene with completely deadpan expressions.","Arisha crossed her arms and sighed. \"Just yesterday, he told me he had changed and wouldn’t chase after women anymore.\"","Lyria stood beside her, watching Noah with a small pout. Her golden hair was tied into her usual braid, which rested over her shoulder. It was a hairstyle Noah secretly liked quite a lot. \"He really is a playboy.\"","\"I always knew he was,\" Emma said with a firm nod.","Leonard clenched his teeth as he watched Noah flirt so effortlessly. \"I wish I had that level of confidence. How does Noah do it? Every time I try talking to a beautiful woman, I lose my voice.\"","\"I don’t know.\" Damien shook his head. \"Maybe he’s just built differently.\"","Kaelan, however, calmly observed Noah for a moment before speaking. \"It’s simple.\" Everyone looked at him. \"Noah doesn’t care whether they reject him or look at him badly. He’s doing it for fun in the first place.\"","Kaelan shrugged. \"He doesn’t actually expect anything from them. That’s why he can say whatever he wants without getting nervous.\"","Leonard’s eyes widened. \"Wow...\" He clenched his fist. \"That bastard is actually enjoying himself.\"","Damien nodded thoughtfully. \"I suppose that’s true. The man doesn’t back down even in front of my master and tease her.\"","He shook his head. \"And sometimes he even gets beaten for it. He truly is impressive in his own strange way.\"","\"Oi, oi.\" Noah who was flirting turned toward them with an annoyed expression. \"I can hear all of you, you know.\"","He clicked his tongue. \"Tch.\"","His friends immediately looked away.","Noah turned back toward the Lunar Elf. For some reason, he decided to make things even worse.","He gently took her hand. Then, with exaggerated elegance, he bent forward and kissed the back of it. The woman’s eyes widened.","\"O-oh my...\" Her face immediately turned bright red. \"Th-this... What is the meaning of this, young man?!\"","Noah straightened with a charming smile. \"It’s a human custom.\" He released her hand. \"We men do that when we meet a particularly beautiful lady who should be cherished.\"","The woman covered her burning face with both hands. \"Oh, goodness! That’s so lewd! holding my hand and kissing it! How can you do such indecent thing!\"","She looked like she wanted to hide behind the counter. \"Young man, I’m dying of embarrassment!\"","Then she suddenly remembered something. \"My husband would be furious if he knew about this!\"","Noah froze. His eyes widened. He immediately released her hand completely and took several steps backward.","\"I-I apologize!\" He bowed deeply. \"I didn’t know you were married.\"","The Lunar Elf remained frozen for a some second, her cheeks were still bright red.","\"I-I am a married elf...\" She lowered her hands slightly. \"And we elves are very loyal...\" Her voice became quieter. \"But...\"","She touched her chest. \"My heart just beat faster because of a human boy...\"","She shook her head rapidly. \"No! No, no, no! I’m such a terrible woman!\"","Noah stared at her. ’Why do I suddenly feel like I’ve entered a romance novel where I’m the villain?’","He slowly backed away. Then he turned toward his friends.","Arisha and Damien were desperately trying to hold back their laughter.","Emma and Leonard were completely frozen, their jaws hanging open and their eyes wide.","Kaelan simply shook his head with the exhausted expression of a man who had already given up trying to understand Noah.","Lyria, meanwhile, clasped both hands together in prayer. \"Please, God, forgive Noah for his sins...\" Her expression was sad, as if apologizing for her own kid. \"He’s still young and a little foolish.\"","Noah’s face twitched. ’Why am I being prayed for like I’m some kind of criminal?!’","He wanted to curse at all of them. But then he looked at Lyria’s innocent expression. His irritation immediately disappeared.","’She’s just too cute...’","Noah quickly shook the thought away.","\"Hey, guys.\"","He forced a smile. \"Let’s get out of here before something worse happens.\"","Just then, \"Dear, I’m back.\""]},{"number":344,"title":"Chapter 344: Four Great Houses","paragraphs":["A male voice came from the entrance of the shop.","Everyone froze as a Lunar Elf man walked into the shop. He had silver hair, pale blue skin, and sharp blue eyes.","Noah’s survival instincts activated instantly as he saw the man. His words instantly gave Noah ideas as who he was.","So he didn’t wait. He turned around and immediately dashed out of the shop, passing the elf man so quickly that the man’s robes fluttered in the wind.","\"Huh?\"","The elf man blinked. \"Why was that young man in such a hurry?\"","He turned around.","Behind him, Noah’s group was already following. One by one, they politely bowed their heads toward him as they passed.","The elf man stared after them.","\"Hm...\"","He glanced at their uniforms. \"Novaris Academy students, perhaps.\"","He shrugged and turned back toward the shop. Then he noticed his wife.","She was standing behind the counter with an extremely red face, her pointed ears twitching nervously.","The elf man’s expression immediately changed. \"What happened?\"","He walked toward her. His wife looked at him. Then she looked around the shop as though she had suddenly returned from another world.","\"Where is that young man?\"","\"What?\"","\"Where did he go?\" She looked toward the entrance. \"He made me feel young again!\"","Her husband stared at her in confusion. \"What are you talking about, dear?!\"","She covered her face again. \"I don’t know!\"","The poor elf man spent the next several minutes trying to calm his wife down and figure out exactly what had happened.","Meanwhile Noah and his friends were already several streets away.","Noah looked over his shoulder. No one was chasing them. He finally let out a sigh of relief.","\"That was close.\"","Arisha immediately burst out laughing. \"Close?! You nearly flirted with a married woman!\"","\"I didn’t know she was married!\"","\"That doesn’t make it better!\" Damien started laughing as well.","Leonard shook his head. \"I can’t believe I witnessed that.\"","Kaelan sighed. \"I told you. He really doesn’t care.\"","Lyria simply smiled helplessly. \"At least you apologized, Noah.\"","Noah nodded seriously. \"Exactly.\" He placed a hand over his chest. \"I’m a responsible gentleman.\"","Everyone stared at him.","\"...\"","Arisha slowly raised an eyebrow.","\"Noah.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"Don’t ever say that again.\"","\"Why?!\"","The entire group burst into laughter.","Noah could only sigh.","\"And now I am more sure that you definitely flirt with Lady Akari in that realm.\" Arisha continued her laugh.","Noah couldn’t help but click his tongue in annoyance.","Somehow, despite everything. He had survived another day without getting beaten by a jealous husband.","---","Noah simply wanted to learn more about the Lunar Elves personally. Unfortunately, there were very few of them living in the city.","He had tried to talk to the elf lady in the perfume shop, but unfortunately, things had gone wrong in a rather strange way.","Who would have thought that his words and actions would have such an impact on a woman who was actually married? It wasn’t entirely his fault, either.","He hadn’t gotten the chance to learn anything about them yet. Asking someone directly was much easier than going to the library and reading about them, especially since Noah hated studying history.","Also Elves had a much lower birth rate compared to humans, largely because of their extraordinarily long lifespans. They had children much later than humans, which naturally resulted in a smaller overall population.","Elythraen also didn’t follow the hierarchical monarchy system used by the human empires.","Instead, the entire nation was ruled by a single monarch—the Queen, or in some eras, a King.","However, beneath the royal family stood four Great Houses.","Much like the four great dukedoms that served under the Emperor of the Aurellian Empire, these four houses governed the major regions of Elythraen and represented its different elven races.","The House Selunaris ruled the southern region, where the Lunar Elves lived. They were known for their mastery of Frost and Lunar Magic.","Then there was House Marisyl, which ruled the eastern coastal region of the continent. They were the great house of the Sea Elves and controlled much of Elythraen’s eastern waters.","In the west was House Nytheris, the great house of the Dark Elves.","And in the north stood House Eldrathil, which governed the vast territories inhabited by the Wood Elves.","Above all four Great Houses stood the royal family—the House Sylvaine, composed primarily of High Elves, also known as Sun Elves.","Noah had researched most of this on his phone the previous night.","Thankfully, the planet’s network was available almost everywhere thanks to the satellites orbiting above them, so even in Elythraen, accessing information through the internet wasn’t a problem.","Unfortunately, the information available online was mostly general knowledge. Noah hadn’t been able to find much about the deeper history of the different elven races or their Great Houses.","But once again, the Lunar Elves had caught his attention.","’Lunar Magic... What exactly is it?’","The question had been bothering him ever since he learned about them.","\"What are you thinking about so deeply, Noah?\"","\"Huh? Nothing, dear.\"","\"H-Hey! Don’t call me dear, Noah!\"","Lyria’s face immediately flushed red as she lightly smacked his shoulder with her palm.","\"Hehe. Sorry~\"","Noah simply grinned before continuing to walk with the others.","The group wandered through the beautiful streets of Lunathiel, taking in the scenery as they explored the elven capital.","\"I’m really interested in learning more about the elves,\" Noah said. \"Do you know where Marina is? She would have been a great help. I heard her family works directly under the royal family and is quite close to them.\"","\"Yes, they are,\" Arisha replied with a nod.","\"She’s with Ken. I saw those two together this morning,\" Damien added casually.","Noah’s expression remained unchanged.","But inwardly, he sighed. ’So, there really is something going on between those two. Ken must be upto something. This is his best chance to meet the Queen. Is he trying to inform her about upcoming danger?’","All Noah could do was wonder and form theories.","---","[A/N: Sigh, curse me!! I really making world more complicated by this. My own brain now hurting. Hope I don’t make it more complicated by loads of information. Pray for it.]"]},{"number":345,"title":"Chapter 345: I’m just admiring the beauty","paragraphs":["Lyria stood on the wooden bridge, leaning lightly against its railing as she gazed at the magnificent World Tree in admiration.","The enormous tree dominated the distant skyline, its vast branches stretching across the sky while countless leaves shimmered beneath the afternoon sunlight.","\"Waiting for me?\"","A voice suddenly whispered beside her ear. Warm breath brushed against her sensitive skin.","\"AEE!?\" Lyria let out a cute yelp and hurriedly stepped away.","Standing behind her was Noah, wearing a teasing smile.","\"Noah! Don’t sneak up on me like that!\" she complained, her fair cheeks already turning bright red. A few strands of her golden hair framed her flushed face.","\"Hehe. Come on, where’s the fun if I can’t tease you?\"","\"Hmm... Noah, you really are...\" Lyria crossed her arms beneath her chest, giving him an exasperated look. Her huge chest looked more prominent because of crossing her arms beneath them.","Noah’s eyes instinctively wandered there for a brief moment before returning to her face, meeting her beautiful pink eyes.","Lyria noticed. Even though it had lasted barely a second, she knew exactly where he had looked. Heat immediately spread across her cheeks.","She was accustomed to people staring at her because of her beauty. It happened often enough that she had learned to ignore it.","Yet somehow, when Noah looked at her like that, it felt strangely more embarrassing.","\"Yo-you! Where exactly do you think you were looking?\"","\"Cough.\" Noah cleared his throat and looked away. \"I apologize. I didn’t mean to stare at... there. It was merely a male reflex when something... that noticeable moves right in front of me—\"","\"Shut up!\"","Lyria’s face became even redder. \"You don’t need to explain yourself!\"","\"Okay, okay... Sorry.\" Noah raised his hands in surrender before glancing around.","\"Anyway, where did everyone else go? I was only gone for a few minutes, and now you’re the only one here.\"","\"They went to the market. We basically split up. Emma and Arisha went to different shops, while Damien and the other boys went somewhere else.\"","\"Oh? And what about you? Didn’t you go with Arisha and Emma?\" Noah asked.","\"I wanted to take a little break, so I decided to wait here for you and the others. We’re all supposed to meet here again later.\"","\"Oh...\" Noah smiled warmly. \"Thank you for waiting for me~\"","He walked toward her with a bright smile.","Lyria could only sigh. By now, she really should have gotten used to his strange way of talking and his constant antics.","She leaned her back against the wooden railing again, relaxing as she looked toward the scenery.","Noah stopped beside her. For a while, neither of them spoke. The people around them continued passing across the bridge, their voices filled with laughter and casual conversation.","A gentle afternoon breeze swept through the city, carrying the faint fragrance of flowers and leaves. Beneath the bridge, the water flowed peacefully, its quiet ripples creating a soothing rhythm.","The enormous trees surrounding around the roads cast cool shadows over parts of the bridge, while golden rays of sunlight slipped through the leaves and painted the wooden walkway in patches of light.","It was a remarkably peaceful atmosphere. Lyria quietly enjoyed the scenery. Then she noticed something.","Noah was staring at her. She could feel his gaze even without looking directly at him. Her cheeks slowly turned pink.","\"No-Noah... why are you staring?\" She finally asked, unable to endure his constant gaze any longer.","Lyria kept her eyes on the scenery, refusing to look at him.","Noah smiled. \"I’m just admiring the beautiful scenery beside me.\" He paused for a moment before adding, \"You look like an innocent saintess standing here on the bridge.\"","\"Huh!?\"","Lyria immediately turned toward him. Her face was bright red. \"You’re doing it again!\"","She lightly smacked his shoulder with her palm. Of course, she didn’t put any real force behind it.","\"Hehe~\" Noah chuckled.","\"You are always messing with me and teasing me!\" She lightly hit his shoulder again. \"Take this!\"","Noah simply laughed as Lyria continued her harmless assault, her embarrassment slowly mixing with amusement.","Under the shade of the World Tree, surrounded by the peaceful sounds of Lunathiel, the two continued their playful bickering as if the rest of the world had momentarily disappeared.","---","\"I am sorry. I couldn’t arrange it.\" Marina lowered her head, her blonde hair falling slightly over her face. \"She’s busy, and apparently, even I can’t meet her right now.\"","The black-haired young man sitting beside her let out a quiet sigh. \"It’s alright. Don’t apologize.\"","Ken’s voice remained calm.","\"Meeting the Queen isn’t something that can be arranged easily. You tried your best. That’s enough for me.\"","The two of them were sitting on a wooden bench beneath the shade of a large tree. The afternoon sunlight filtered through the leaves, casting shifting patterns of light across the ground.","\"But tomorrow, when we go to see the World Tree from up close, Her Majesty, Queen Aelyssa, will be there.\"","\"True...\" Ken’s gray eyes narrowed slightly. \"But that doesn’t mean I’ll be able to talk to her.\"","\"Yes, but I can.\" Marina looked at him. \"She might allow me to speak with her privately. If that happens, I can take you with me.\"","Ken stared at her for several seconds.","His gray eyes revealed nothing about what he was thinking. Marina couldn’t tell whether he was surprised, relieved, or already considering something else entirely.","\"Then I guess... we should try that.\"","Marina nodded. \"Yes. I’ll do my best. After all, because of you, my sister might finally be cured.\"","\"It’s alright.\" Ken’s expression softened slightly. \"You’re my friend.\"","Marina smiled faintly. \"...But can you really not tell me what you want to talk to her about?\"","Ken didn’t answer immediately. He looked at Marina for a long moment before finally speaking.","\"Well, you see...\" He paused. \"There’s a very high chance that something dangerous will happen on the final day of our trip.\"","Marina’s eyes widened. \"What?\"","She leaned forward. \"How can you say that? Is there going to be another attack on us Academy students?\"","Ken remained silent. The silence itself made Marina even more uneasy.","\"Ken?\"","He finally looked at her. \"Do you believe me?\"","Marina hesitated. There was something strange about the way he asked that question. Still, after a moment, she nodded.","\"Yes. I do.\" Ken lowered his gaze. \"The attack or whatever is going to happen—won’t exactly be directed at the students.\"","\"Then... who?\"","\"You could say...\" He paused again. \"We’re simply here at the wrong time.\"","Marina’s expression became serious. \"So it’s related to the elves of this city?\"","Ken didn’t answer.","\"Are they in danger?\" She asked.","\"The thing is...\" His voice became more serious as he started to tell her.","Neither of them noticed the faint figure standing on a distant rooftop, watching them from afar."]},{"number":346,"title":"Chapter 346: Eldrian Vaelwood","paragraphs":["Several hours later.","The sun had disappeared beyond the horizon, and Lunathiel had transformed beneath the evening sky.","The magical lamps illuminating the streets had replaced the afternoon sunlight, their gentle glow reflecting against the countless trees and elegant wooden buildings.","The city was still lively.","People walked through the streets, merchants called out to customers, and groups of elves gathered around restaurants and cafés to enjoy their evening.","Meanwhile, Noah and his friends had settled inside a cozy café near one of the main streets.","\"Ahh... this coffee is pretty good.\"","Damien leaned back in his chair, holding his cup with both hands.","Emma nodded enthusiastically. \"Right? I didn’t expect elven coffee to taste this good.\"","\"I told you elves had good taste,\" Arisha said casually.","Leonard took another sip before glancing around the café. \"Everything here is so different from the places in the Empire.\"","Kaelan nodded. \"Their architecture, magical technology, even the way they use natural materials. It’s surprisingly sophisticated.\"","Noah listened to them while quietly enjoying his own coffee.","Their table was surrounded by the warm glow of magical lamps. Beyond the large windows, Lunathiel continued to shine beneath the night sky.","Lyria sat beside Noah, occasionally joining the conversation.","For once, Noah wasn’t teasing her.","He simply enjoyed the peaceful atmosphere.","After everything that had happened since their arrival, this was probably the first time he had been able to relax properly.","He slowly raised his cup. Then, for some reason, his gaze drifted toward the window. His hand stopped halfway.","\"Hm?\"","Someone was standing outside.","Noah narrowed his eyes. Across the street, beside the outer wall of a large building, stood a familiar figure.","Green hair, dark-green robe and calm expression on face. It was Eldrian Vaelwood. One of the elves assigned to guide their group during their stay in Elythraen.","But something felt strange. Eldrian wasn’t doing anything.","He was simply standing there, his back resting lightly against the wall as he gazed toward the street.","Noah stared at him for a few seconds. ’Why is he standing there alone this late?’","Eldrian suddenly turned his head. For a brief moment, their eyes met through the café window.","Noah’s expression remained calm.","Eldrian’s expression didn’t change either. But something about his gaze made Noah feel as though he had been caught watching him.","Then Eldrian looked away. Noah slowly lowered his cup.","\"What is it, Noah?\"","Lyria noticed his sudden change in expression.","Noah didn’t answer immediately.","His eyes remained fixed on the building across the street.","\"...Nothing.\"","He smiled faintly.","\"Just thought I saw something interesting.\"","But inwardly, his thoughts were already racing. ’Why do I have a feeling that something is about to happen?’ He got up from the seat.","\"What happened?\" Damien asked Noah.","\"Nothing, bro. I just saw Sir Eldrian outside. I wanted to ask him a few things, so I’ll go talk to him.\"","Without waiting for anyone else to respond, Noah stood up and left the café.","He crossed the road, his eyes remaining on the elf standing against the wall of the building opposite them.","Eldrian noticed him approaching and turned his head. When Noah stopped in front of him, the elf spoke.","\"Is there something you need from me, young man?\"","Noah gave him a polite smile. \"Actually, I wanted to talk to someone knowledgeable about elves. I’ve become quite interested in elven culture and history since coming here.\"","\"Oh?\" Eldrian’s expression brightened slightly. \"It’s always good to see young people taking an interest in our history and cultures. What would you like to know?\"","\"Hehe. Well, first of all, you can just call me Noah. I’m Noah Eldritch.\"","\"Eldritch?\" Eldrian’s eyebrows rose in surprise.","\"Now that’s something I didn’t expect. You’re from one of the four great ducal houses of the human empire, the House Eldritch.\"","\"Yes. I’m the youngest son.\"","Eldrian immediately straightened his posture and gave a slight bow. \"Then I should properly greet someone from—\"","\"Wait, you don’t need to do that, Sir Eldrian.\" Noah quickly stopped him. \"I’m just a student here. I’m not here as the son of some great family.\"","Eldrian looked at him for a moment before smiling. \"If you insist.\" He relaxed his posture again. \"So, what was it you wanted to ask me?\"","\"Well...\" Noah looked at him curiously. \"Are you a Wood Elf?\"","\"Yes, I am.\" Eldrian smiled.","\"Wow. I’ve already met a Lunar Elf and a Wood Elf today, but I haven’t had the chance to meet elves from the other races.\"","\"That’s only natural.\"","Eldrian chuckled. \"Sun Elves rarely leave the capital’s central territories, especially members of the royal family. Sea Elves mostly remain within their own regions as well, while Dark Elves tend to stay in their western territories.\"","\"Hmm...\" Noah nodded thoughtfully. \"So you’re originally from the northern region, the territory governed by House Eldrathil. When did you come to Lunathiel?\"","\"It’s been about forty years since I came here.\"","\"Forty years?\"","\"Yes. My family sent me here to join the royal family’s military forces in the capital.\"","Eldrian’s expression became slightly proud. \"For an Elf, serving the royal family is considered a great honor.\"","\"So you’ve been living here for forty years?\"","\"That’s right.\"","\"Do you live alone?\"","\"No.\" Eldrian smiled. \"I have a daughter. She’s only eight years old.\"","He paused for a moment.","Noah waited patiently, but when Eldrian remained silent, he glanced at him. \"And... just your daughter?\"","\"Yes.\" Eldrian’s expression softened. \"I live with her here. I once tried to send her back to my family’s territory in the north, where she would have been surrounded by relatives and other children.\"","He gave a small, helpless smile. \"But she refused to leave my side.\" There was warmth in his eyes as he spoke about his daughter. \"You might be wondering about my wife.\"","Noah remained silent. \"She passed away six years ago.\"","Eldrian’s voice remained calm, though a trace of sadness could be heard beneath it. \"She was killed by a demon.\"","Noah’s expression immediately became serious. \"I’m sorry to hear that.\"","Eldrian smiled gently. \"It’s alright. She was also a member of the royal defense forces.\"","He looked toward the distant streets of Lunathiel. \"That night, I had taken the night off so I could stay home and look after our daughter. My wife, however, was on duty with her squad.\"","His expression darkened slightly. \"They encountered a group of demons that had somehow crossed into our territory. She and the others fought them...\"","He paused. \"And she never came home. But as a protector of this city I am proud of her.\"","Noah didn’t know what to say. He had only intended to ask a few questions about elven culture. Somehow, the conversation had turned into something much more personal than he had expected.","’Look at me... I barely know this man, and somehow I ended up learning about his entire family.’","Noah scratched his cheek awkwardly. Still, he didn’t want to abruptly change the subject after Eldrian had shared something so painful.","Eldrian seemed to notice his hesitation and chuckled. \"Don’t worry about it. I don’t mind talking about her.\"","Noah nodded. \"I understand.\"","Then he smiled. \"I’d actually like to meet your daughter someday. She must be a cute little girl.\"","\"Hehe. Yes, she is.\" Eldrian’s face immediately softened. \"She’s a wonderful child. And she’s already decided what she wants to become when she grows up.\"","\"Really? What does she want to be?\"","\"An archer.\" Eldrian laughed softly. \"She wants to become an archer just like her mother.\"","Noah fell silent for a moment. There was something strangely touching about that. A daughter following in the footsteps of a mother she had lost far too young.","Noah looked at Eldrian.","There was still one question that had been occupying his mind ever since he first learned about the different elven races.","He hesitated briefly before finally asking. \"I... wanted to ask you something I’ve been really curious about.\"","Eldrian turned toward him.","\"What is it?\"","Noah looked toward the distant World Tree before returning his gaze to the Wood Elf. \"Lunar Magic.\"","His eyes narrowed slightly with curiosity. \"What exactly is Lunar Magic? Is it something that only Lunar elves can use?\"","---","[A/N: Shameless author strikes again with a very enticing offer!","Do you want more Chapters?","I have a solution!","Complete the quests below to receive bonus Chapters as rewards:","1. Golden Tickets:","For every 50 Golden Tickets, receive 1 bonus Chapter.","2. Gifts:","For every 1,000 Coins gifted, receive 1 bonus Chapter.","3. Super Gifts:","I have decided to divide Super Gifts into three categories:","3(i). Magic Castle:","3 Chapters/day for an entire week.","3(ii). Spacecraft:","Choose between:","3 Chapters/day for two weeks or","4 Chapters/day for one week.","The decision is left to the Blessed Reader who sends the gift.","3(iii). Golden Gachapon:","Choose between:","3 Chapters/day for one month or","4 Chapters/day for two weeks.","Again, the decision will be made by the Blessed Reader.","So... what are you waiting for?","Complete your quests and claim your bonus Chapters while helping this poor author earn some extra bucks in the process.","◉⁠‿⁠◉]"]}]);
